    "md5": "268ac040d869148cd13fe03c48d353da",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1975,
    "chunk_text": "UN Global Compact launches coalition to take sustainability into SL boardrooms\n\nThe UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka has launched a new private-sector coalition, aimed at integrating sustainability, stronger governance and responsible business practices into corporate boardrooms and executive decision-making.\n\nThe Responsible Business Coalition will bring together the business and professional institutions to promote the UN Global Compact\u2019s Ten Principles across Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate sector through advocacy, technical capacity-building, strategic engagements and shared learning.\n\nIts founding members include the Sri Lanka Bankers\u2019 Association\u2019s Sustainable Banking Initiative, Sri Lanka Institute of Directors and Centre for a Smart Future.\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE) and The Ceylon Chamber of Commerce are supporting the initiative and working towards founding membership, according to the UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka.\n\nThe coalition is intended to move responsible business practices beyond the companies\u2019 dedicated sustainability functions and integrate them into board-level governance, executive leadership and professional development.\n\nThe initiative was launched during UN Global Compact CEO and Executive Director Sanda Ojiambo\u2019s visit to Sri Lanka.\n\nThe launch coincided with a \u2018Ring the Bell for Responsible Business\u2019 ceremony at the CSE, where Ojiambo joined the exchange\u2019s senior leadership to ring the opening bell.\n\nAddressing the event, Ojiambo said responsible business was increasingly becoming a strategic requirement for competitiveness, trust and long-term value creation rather than merely a corporate responsibility exercise.\n\n\u201cThe private sector has a critical role to play in shaping economies that are resilient, inclusive and sustainable. As businesses navigate a rapidly changing global landscape, responsible business is increasingly central to competitiveness, trust and long-term value creation.\u201d"
  },
