    "chunk_text": "\u201cNPP which came with many promises is dragging country towards a dictatorship\u201d  MP Ranjith Madduma Bandara\n\n\u201cIt is evident that this government will amend the constitution to fulfill their political needs\u201d- MP Ranjith Madduma Bandara\n\nAlso a 2.5 Million dollar scandal occurred and the Minister of Finance, who is the President, should be responsible\n\nWe had that particular discussion with Ranil along with other parties against the politicisation of the judiciary\n\nGeneral Secretary of Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Ranjith Madduma Bandara in an interview with Daily Mirror stated that his party will be forming an alliance with UNP for upcoming elections.He stated that the government has failed to deliver on the promises given to the public and is driving the country towards a dictatorship. He further stated that the government\u2019s inability to take actions against members and associates of their party who are alleged of corruption and crimes is questionable.\n\nQ While the opposition alleges that the popularity of the government is lost, there is an equally weak opposition. Being the main opposition party, what is\u00a0your response?"
