    "md5": "8c52375ff99121c545439cbe5636eccc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1943,
    "chunk_text": "We are content with our decision as SJB won 60 seats at the parliamentary elections while the UNP was able to secure only one seat. Also, we became the main opposition party. This means the decision we took was correct. Today, irrespective of the voters\u2019 strength of the UNP, the people have requested both the parties to join. We will be\u00a0forming an Alliance.\n\nQRecently we saw Ranil Wickremesinghe returning to the Opposition Head office. What was the discussion about? Was is about the alliance? Where would Ranil stand in the UNP, SJB or in the Opposition?\n\nWe are merely forming an alliance with the UNP for the upcoming elections. Legally, a member of the SJB cannot become a member of the UNP and the same applies for the members of the UNP.\n\n\u201cThe coal procurement scam is one of the major scandals that happened. It is the opposition who revealed this to the public. As a result, the government was compelled to remove the Secretary and the Minister. These issues show how corrupt the government is and how weak they are\n\nQ The recent judgment against former IGP and Defence Secretary relating to the Easter Sunday attacks have proved there had been major miscommunications, mishaps and negligence with regard to National Security under your government. Where did it go wrong?\n\nYes, we were in power when the Easter attacks occurred. Before the constitutional coup which took place, I was the Minister of Law and Order. But at the time of the Easter Attacks took place the Minister of Law and Order was then President Maithripala Sirisena. As per my knowledge and understanding SIS reports are sent to the President and to the Minister of Public Security, the IGP and the Secretary of the Ministry of Law and Order. Other officials of the government were not informed about this.\n\nI will refrain from commenting about the judicial decision. We request the government to find the perpetrators of this crime and\u00a0bring them to court."
