    "md5": "3a31b14527518ef21bd44d440875ce6f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1522,
    "chunk_text": "In her address to the trading floor, Ojiambo highlighted the increasingly important role of the private sector in building resilient, inclusive and sustainable economies, noting that responsible business is no longer simply a matter of corporate responsibility, but a strategic imperative for long-term competitiveness and resilience.\n\nOjiambo further emphasised the important role of stock exchanges and listed companies in mobilising sustainable finance and accelerating progress towards the Sustainable Development Goals, reaffirming the Ten Principles of the UN Global Compact as a globally recognised framework for advancing responsible business practices.\n\nA key highlight of the morning was the official launch of the Responsible Business Coalition, convened by UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka. The Coalition brings together leading business and professional institutions to accelerate the integration of responsible business practices beyond sustainability functions and into boardrooms, executive leadership and professional development. Through coordinated advocacy, strategic convening, technical capacity-building and shared learning, the Coalition will strengthen the adoption of the Ten Principles of the UN Global Compact across Sri Lanka\u2019s corporate landscape.\n\nCommenting on the significance of the initiative, the Colombo Stock Exchange highlighted the importance of collaboration between capital market institutions and the wider business community in advancing sustainable and responsible growth."
  },
