    "chunk_text": "Commenting on the significance of the initiative, the Colombo Stock Exchange highlighted the importance of collaboration between capital market institutions and the wider business community in advancing sustainable and responsible growth.\n\nThe Coalition\u2019s founding members at present include the Sri Lanka Bankers\u2019 Association \u2013 Sustainable Banking Initiative (SLBA-SBI), Sri Lanka Institute of Directors (SLID), and the Centre for Smart Future. Supporters of the Coalition, working towards founding membership, include the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), Ceylon Chamber of Commerce (CCC). Together, these institutions represent a powerful coalition committed to embedding responsible business practices across Sri Lanka\u2019s private sector.\n\nSpeaking on the significance of the initiative, representatives of UN Global Compact Network Sri Lanka noted that the Responsible Business Coalition represents a collective commitment to move beyond individual organisational efforts and foster a coordinated national movement for responsible business. By leveraging the reach and influence of Sri Lanka\u2019s leading professional and business associations, the Coalition will equip current and future business leaders with the knowledge, tools and partnerships needed to advance the Ten Principles and accelerate progress towards the SDGs.\n\nThe Ring the Bell ceremony forms part of a globally recognised initiative led by entities including the UN Sustainable Stock Exchanges Initiative, UN Global Compact, International Finance Corporation (IFC) and the World Federation of Exchanges, demonstrating the critical role that capital markets play in advancing sustainable development."
