    "chunk_text": "The cultural programme also featured Tari Tor Tor, a traditional dance of the Batak community of North Sumatra. The performance was presented by dancers from the Sanka Samudhi Performing Art Foundation of Kalutara, highlighting Indonesia's rich performing arts traditions.\n\nTogether, the performances from Java, North Sumatra and Bali showcased the cultural diversity of Indonesia. The participation of Sri Lankan musicians and dancers alongside Indonesian diplomatic staff also demonstrated how cultural activities can encourage artistic collaboration and mutual understanding between the two countries.\n\nThe performances were warmly received by the audience, with particular appreciation for the involvement of Sri Lankan artists in presenting Indonesian traditional arts.\n\nThe ICC is expected to offer a range of programmes for the Sri Lankan public, including Indonesian language courses, traditional Indonesian dance classes and classes on traditional Indonesian musical instruments.\n\nThe centre will also organise workshops, exhibitions, traditional arts performances, film screenings and other cultural exchange programmes, providing Sri Lankans with opportunities to engage directly with Indonesian culture."
