    "chunk_size_bytes": 1527,
    "chunk_text": "The Mecca pact also exposed the unreliability of the United States as a security partner. Saudi Arabia has bitter experience with Washington, which failed to respond to drone and cruise\u2011missile attacks on Saudi oil facilities in September, allegedly carried out by Iran. Saudi Arabia was shocked when Israel struck a residential facility housing a Hamas peace delegation in Qatar last year, with the US maintaining strategic ignorance, thus abandoning Qatar despite close defence ties. Moreover, when the Iran war broke out, Washington was unable to provide security cover to regional countries, even as it relied on bases and radar facilities in those countries to attack Iran.\n\nThe Mecca agreement follows a failed Saudi attempt between 2015 and 2017 to form a pan\u2011Islamic military coalition against the backdrop of Yemen\u2019s civil war. The August 7 deal emerged after a top\u2011secret initiative by Ankara, which has not taken lightly Israel\u2019s recent comments describing T\u00fcrkiye as a security threat.\n\nThe Mecca security alliance is reinforced by Saudi Arabia\u2019s financial strength and strategic geography, stretching east to west from the Strait of Hormuz to the Red Sea; T\u00fcrkiye\u2019s military weight as an advanced arms manufacturer; and Pakistan\u2019s ability to provide the much\u2011needed nuclear umbrella.\n\nThe deal signals the formalisation of the close security relations that T\u00fcrkiye and Saudi Arabia already had with Pakistan. It also expands on the agreement Islamabad and Riyadh signed in September last year."
  },
