    "chunk_size_bytes": 1133,
    "chunk_text": "The deal signals the formalisation of the close security relations that T\u00fcrkiye and Saudi Arabia already had with Pakistan. It also expands on the agreement Islamabad and Riyadh signed in September last year.\n\nRegarded as the mother country of Sunni Islam, Saudi Arabia sits atop a military power mine it does not know how to harness or strategise. If Ray Klein\u2019s formula is applied to measure Saudi Arabia\u2019s power, what it lacks is strategic population strength and the political will to resist \u2014 elements that can come only through the Islamisation of security, as Iran has done. Iran\u2019s security solutions are home\u2011grown and faith\u2011driven, whereas Saudi Arabia depends on Western solutions, particularly from the United States, which is certain to side with Israel should war erupt between Israel and Saudi Arabia.\n\nIslamisation of security offers Saudi Arabia a two\u2011billion\u2011strong global military force. Meanwhile, the Mecca security deal could emerge as a greater deterrent against Israel and ensure regional stability if it can bring Iran into the fold or establish a separate regional security pact with Tehran."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
