    "md5": "39d9bb6c1cf261d87bd4a97943a27396",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1774,
    "chunk_text": "SEC, CSE  to host \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 forum from 17-20 Aug. in Australia\n\nThe Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC), Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), and the stock broking industry are conducting a series of \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 investor forums in Australia, with multiple forums to be held in Melbourne and Sydney. The forums will be held in Sydney and Melbourne from 17 August 2026 to 20 August 2026.\n\nThe \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 Investor Forum \u2013 Australia 2026 follows the \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 Investor Forums held in Dubai and Riyadh earlier in January.\u00a0 Capitalising\u00a0 on the growth and stability achieved in the Sri Lankan capital market in 2025, the \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 investor forums of 2026 are set to leverage on Sri Lanka\u2019s status as an attractive frontier market and will seek to attract institutional investors and the Sri Lankan diaspora.\n\nThe SEC and CSE will be returning to Australia after nearly nine years following the last \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 Investor Forum Australia conducted in 2017. The 2017 roadshow played an important role in strengthening investor awareness of Sri Lanka among investors in Australia, with buy turnover rising over 700% from Rs. 72.9 million to Rs. 603.8 million within the six-month window following the forums.\n\nAs of the end of 2025 buy turnover has risen to Rs. 1.85 billion with Australia emerging as one of the top 10 sources of foreign investor inflows into the Sri Lankan capital market, and as one of the top 10 sources of remittance inflows from the growing Sri Lankan diaspora in Australia.\u00a0 With the strong rise in Sri Lanka\u2019s All-Share-Price-Index (ASPI) over the past 10 years, a rising number of Sri Lankan diaspora investors have taken an interest in the Sri Lankan stock market."
  },
