    "chunk_text": "As of the end of 2025 buy turnover has risen to Rs. 1.85 billion with Australia emerging as one of the top 10 sources of foreign investor inflows into the Sri Lankan capital market, and as one of the top 10 sources of remittance inflows from the growing Sri Lankan diaspora in Australia.\u00a0 With the strong rise in Sri Lanka\u2019s All-Share-Price-Index (ASPI) over the past 10 years, a rising number of Sri Lankan diaspora investors have taken an interest in the Sri Lankan stock market.\n\nSEC Chairman Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara said: \u201cSri Lanka is strengthening its capital market through robust regulation, greater transparency and stronger investor protection, creating a more trusted and resilient environment for investors. We invite Australian investors to explore the opportunities emerging in our market.\u201d\n\nHigh-level government officials, regulators, listed companies, leading stock brokering firms, and international investors will convene at the forum to foster connections and promote long-term capital flows into Sri Lanka. CSE Vice President \u2013 Marketing Niroshan Wijesundere commented that there is strong interest in the forums, with registrations for several sessions already exceeding capacity.\n\nCHEC Port City Colombo is participating in the Invest Sri Lanka Investor Forums in Australia as a collaborative partner, joining the SEC and the CSE in bringing Sri Lanka\u2019s investment proposition to Australian investors and businesses.\n\nCHEC Port City Colombo Ltd., Managing Director Xiong Hongfeng said:\u00a0 \u201cAustralia represents a significant market for Sri Lanka, and this forum provides a timely platform to engage directly with investors who are well-positioned to recognise the opportunity. We look forward to sharing what Port City Colombo has to offer as part of Sri Lanka\u2019s broader investment story.\u201d"
