    "md5": "81d5e63864edde97f28b39e1d58ac596",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1616,
    "chunk_text": "JICA Senior Vice President Hara visits Sri Lanka\n\nJICA Senior Vice President Shohei Hara with Prime Minister\u00a0Dr. Harini Amarasuriya\n\nFrom left: JICA Sri Lanka Chief Representative Shigeo Honzu, UN Assistant Secretary-General and UN Global Compact CEO Sanda Ojiambo, JICA Senior Vice President Shohei Hara, and Global Compact Network Sri Lanka Executive Director Rathika de Silva\n\nJapan International Cooperation Agency (JICA) Senior Vice President Shohei Hara visited Sri Lanka this week to meet with senior Government officials and development partners and to discuss future cooperation in support of Sri Lanka\u2019s sustainable development and economic recovery.\n\nOn 11 August, Hara met with Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya, Treasury Secretary Dr. Harshana Suriyapperuma together with senior officials of the Finance Ministry, and other key stakeholders to exchange views on Sri Lanka\u2019s development priorities and future cooperation between Sri Lanka and Japan.\n\nDuring the meetings, Hara conveyed JICA\u2019s condolences to those affected by Cyclone Ditwah and reaffirmed Japan\u2019s continued commitment to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery and sustainable development. Discussions also covered Sri Lanka\u2019s facilitation of smooth implementation of on-going JICA supported projects, and opportunities and instruments to further strengthen bilateral cooperation.\n\nHara also met with United Nations Assistant Secretary-General and the United Nations Global Compact CEO Sanda Ojiambo and exchanged views on sustainable development and partnerships for achieving the Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)."
  },
