    "chunk_text": "SLFPA President Aruna Senanayake said: \u201cWe remain deeply committed to supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s small and medium-scale food processors, who represent the backbone of our industry. The SME Pavilion, organised by the Industries Ministry has attracted a significant number of SMEs in previous years and provided tremendous support by bringing together many SME exhibitors under one roof for this mega event. This exhibition will provide SMEs with a valuable opportunity to showcase their innovations, gain market exposure and receive valuable feedback from end consumers.\u201d\n\nProFood ProPack and AgBiz 2026 Organising Committee Co-Chairmen Nadishan Guruge and Sameera Jayathilake said: \u201cProFood ProPack and AgBiz has grown into a key platform that brings together the entire food processing, packaging and agriculture ecosystem, creating opportunities for innovation, collaboration, and business development. This year\u2019s edition will further elevate the experience by expanding international participation, showcasing emerging technologies and providing dedicated platforms for startups, SMEs and industry professionals to connect with potential partners and consumers. We believe this exhibition will continue to play an important role in supporting the growth and competitiveness of Sri Lanka\u2019s food and agriculture sectors while opening new avenues for knowledge exchange and investments.\u201d\n\nWith its expanded international participation, comprehensive exhibition showcase and knowledge-driven program, ProFood ProPack and AgBiz 2026 is set to reinforce Sri Lanka\u2019s position as a growing hub for food processing, packaging and agricultural innovation while creating new opportunities for sustainable industry development, investment, and collaboration."
