    "description": "CSE-SEC launch \u2018A Share for Everyone, A Unit for Everyone\u2019 initiative",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/CSE-SEC-launch-A-Share-for-Everyone-A-Unit-for-Everyone-initiative/215-348088",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1786685301.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-14-dailymirrorlk-f9f2ed6c-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "45480cb7bc6f5e678bb06ab74481b55b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1839,
    "chunk_text": "CSE-SEC launch \u2018A Share for Everyone, A Unit for Everyone\u2019 initiative\n\nMonaragala Investor Forum panel discussion members from left: Softlogic Asset Management Manager Business Development Kumudu Kekirideniya, HNB Stockbrokers Director Sales Kapila Pathirage, CSE Executive Vice President Marketing Niroshan Wijesundere and SEC Manager External Relations Nimal Kumarasinghe\n\nThe Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), together with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC) launched its \u2018A Share for Everyone, A Unit for Everyone\u2019 initiative at the investor forums in Monaragala and Batticaloa recently as part of an ongoing islandwide initiative to broaden investor participation.\n\nThe forums were held in Monaragala at Silanrich Hotel and in Batticaloa at FG Golden River Hotel. The forums attracted over 500 participants across both locations.\n\nThe \u2018A Share for Everyone, A Unit for Everyone\u2019 concept, developed by SEC Chairman Sen. Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, aims to promote a shared commitment to creating wealth and value within a fair, efficient, orderly and transparent capital market by ensuring broad and accessible participation for all.\n\nThe investor forums opened with presentations by senior economists from the Central Bank, including N.B. Janagan and Kasunka Herath, who provided a high-level overview of the country\u2019s macroeconomic landscape.\n\nFirst Capital Holdings Vice President Corporate Finance and Advisory Atchuthan Srirangan and HNB Stockbrokers Director Sales Kapila Pathirage offered the participants an overview of the capital market and its investment opportunities.\n\nSoftlogic Asset Management Manager Business Development Kumudu Kekirideniya and Softlogic Asset Management Business Development Officer Mohamed Ashfer introduced participants to the fundamentals of unit trust investing."
  },
