    "md5": "6e4c1c9a8dcba5aa2368e6418837574b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1819,
    "chunk_text": "SLRA-PIM inaugurate Retail Leadership Development Programme\u2019s 2nd batch\n\nOfficial inauguration of SLRA-PIM Retail Leadership Development Programme Batch Two\n\nThe Sri Lanka Retailers\u2019 Association (SLRA), in collaboration with the Postgraduate Institute of Management (PIM), officially inaugurated the second batch of the SLRA-PIM Retail Leadership Development Programme, at the PIM, marking another significant milestone in strengthening leadership capabilities within Sri Lanka\u2019s retail industry.\n\nBuilding on the success of its inaugural cohort, the programme has attracted an exceptional response from the retail sector, with nominations exceeding the available intake. The overwhelming interest highlights the industry\u2019s growing recognition of the importance of investing in leadership development to build resilient, future-ready organisations.\n\nThe inauguration ceremony brought together senior representatives from leading retail organisations, industry professionals and academia, underscoring the collaborative commitment to nurturing the next generation of retail leaders.\n\nThe head table comprised PIM Director Dr. Asanga Ranasinghe, PIM Senior Lecturer Dr. Samantha Rathnayake, SLRA President Infiyaz Ali, SLRA Immediate Past President Charitha Subasinghe and SLRA Senior Vice President Mahesh Wijewardene.\n\nThe event featured the official inauguration of the programme, an introductory briefing outlining the curriculum and learning journey and networking opportunities among the participants and representatives from Sri Lanka\u2019s leading retail organisations.\n\nThe programme has been designed to create a platform where emerging retail leaders can gain practical knowledge, exchange experiences and develop the leadership capabilities required to navigate an increasingly dynamic retail landscape."
