    "chunk_size_bytes": 1648,
    "chunk_text": "Port City Colombo brings SL\u2019s South Asian investment proposition to Maldives\n\nThe High Commission of Sri Lanka in the Republic of Maldives, in collaboration with CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt.) Ltd, hosted the Port City Colombo Investor Forum at Barcel\u00f3 Nasandhura Mal\u00e9 on August 10, 2026, an invitation-only engagement bringing together a curated gathering of senior Maldivian business leaders, investors and developers.\n\nThe forum marks a significant step in the deepening economic relationship between Sri Lanka and the Maldives and continues Port City Colombo\u2019s structured programme of regional investor engagement, following the successful forums in Singapore, the UAE and Oman this year.\n\nIt offered the Maldivian business and investment leaders a first-hand opportunity to learn about Port City Colombo\u2019s investment proposition, Sri Lanka\u2019s flagship 269-hectare master-planned city and Special Economic Zone (SEZ) and to explore how it can serve as a practical platform for the Maldivian businesses and investors seeking to expand their presence across South Asia.\n\nOpening the forum, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to the Republic of Maldives Mohamed Rizvi Hassen set the tone for a morning of substantive dialogue, reflecting on the depth and natural complementarity of the Sri Lanka\u2013Maldives bilateral relationship.\n\nHe noted that Sri Lanka and the Maldives are among the Indian Ocean\u2019s closest neighbours connected by geography, culture and long-standing people-to-people ties and that Port City Colombo represents a tangible and timely opportunity to translate that relationship into a new dimension of economic partnership."
  },
