    "chunk_size_bytes": 786,
    "chunk_text": "Heat index likely to reach \u2018Caution\u2019 level in seven districts\n\nColombo, August 14 (Daily Mirror) - The heat index, or the temperature felt by the human body, is expected to rise to the \u2018Caution\u2019 level in several areas of seven districts during the daytime, the Department of Meteorology warned.\n\nThe advisory applies to Vavuniya, Mullaitivu, Trincomalee, Polonnaruwa, Batticaloa, Ampara and Monaragala districts.\n\nResidents in the affected areas are advised to remain cautious during the daytime, particularly when engaging in outdoor activities, as the combination of high temperatures and humidity could increase heat-related risks.\n\nThe public is advised to stay hydrated, avoid prolonged exposure to direct sunlight and take adequate precautions during periods of high heat."
  },
