    "md5": "fac2733ce5074dc928bdb0a071c4fdbc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1665,
    "chunk_text": "RCSS Commemorates Prof. Shelton Kodikara\n\nAmerican University, Washington, D.C., Distinguished Professor of International Relations and UNESCO Chair in Transnational Challenges and Governance Prof. Amitav Acharya\n\nFormer President, BNMF and BCIS Council of Management Chairperson Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga\n\nLeading global IR scholar Prof. Amitav Acharya delivers memorial oration\n\nThe \u2018Professor Shelton U. Kodikara Memorial Oration\u2019 organised by the Regional Centre for Strategic Studies (RCSS), in collaboration with the Bandaranaike Centre for International Studies (BCIS), was held on 8 August 2026 at the BCIS auditorium.\n\nCommemorating the pioneer of the study of International Relations in Sri Lanka and the founder of the RCSS, it brought together friends and family of the late Professor, diplomats, public officials, academics, policymakers, other distinguished invitees and students of international relations.\n\nAt the commencement, a floral tribute was offered in memory of Prof. Kodikara by his son Dilip Kodikara, a Founder member of the RCSS Board of Directors, and a commemorative video reflecting the legacy of Prof. Kodikara was presented.\n\nIn the keynote address, the Chief Guest Former President, BNMF and BCIS Council of Management Chairperson Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga recalled that Prof. Kodikara was not merely an academic, but a leader of Sri Lanka\u2019s national intellectual identity. Noting that in much of our post-independence history, our foreign policy was practiced in what may be called a void of academic expertise where the praxis of diplomacy prevailed over scholarship, she said Prof. Kodikara changed that."
  },
