    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Every day, thousands of conversations happen online; people share opinions, review products, and react to brands in real time. Social intelligence helps organizations understand those conversations and identify what matters. It is not just about counting mentions or likes. It is about understanding why people are talking, their underlying feelings, and emerging trends to guide strategic decisions. Basically, it is about listening before speaking.\n\nQ Has the role of public relations evolved alongside this trend?\n\nAbsolutely. The biggest change is our shift from being reactive to highly proactive. Instead of relying solely on post-campaign reports, we now monitor real-time conversations, anticipate potential issues, and provide strategic advice before they evolve into larger challenges.\n\nQ Mark&Comm has introduced Talkwalker to the Sri Lankan market. What makes it different?\n\nTalkwalker allows us to monitor conversations across news outlets, social media, forums, and other online sources simultaneously. Locally, it is highly capable of extracting data in Sinhala, Tamil, and Singlish. However, the real value lies in what we do with that information. We analyze patterns, measure sentiment, benchmark competitors, and turn data into practical recommendations. Technology provides the intelligence, but our team\u2019s expertise transforms it into a meaningful strategy.\n\nQHow can corporations get their hands on this intelligence, and is there an opportunity to experience it first?\n\nCorporates can access this through Mark&Comm as a fully managed service. Clients do not need to operate the enterprise platform themselves; we handle the real-time monitoring, data extraction, and strategic analysis. We also offer a seven-day trial period, giving potential clients the opportunity to see exactly what the tool can do and understand if it provides specific, actionable insights before making a long-term commitment."
