    "chunk_text": "The Board of Investment of Sri Lanka will also be participating in the forums, further strengthening the representation of key stakeholders driving the country\u2019s investment and economic development agenda.\n\nThe speakers and panellists at the events include Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Deputy Minister Chathuranga Abeysinghe, Central Bank Governor Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe, High Commissioner of Sri Lanka to Australia Yasoja Gunesekara, SEC Chairman Senior Prof D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, CSE Director Ray Abeywardena, Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Director General Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena, Consul General of Sri Lanka to Victoria, South Australia and Tasmania Pradeepa Saram, CSE CEO Rajeeva Bandaranaike, Lynear Wealth Management Co-Founder and Managing Director Dr. Naveen Gunawardane, ACP Corum Pty Ltd Executive Director Charles Blake, Hatton National Bank PLC Managing Director and CEO Damith Pallewatte and CHEC Port City Colombo Deputy Managing Director Thulci Aluwihare.\n\nAll of them will be sharing their insights, highlighting the country\u2019s ongoing economic reforms, financial stability and capital market potential through a series of panel discussions and presentations. The registered participants will get the opportunity to access to a series of sessions offering in-depth insights into Sri Lanka\u2019s capital markets, economic outlook and investment opportunities. The programme will also feature a high-level panel discussion, featuring leaders and market experts who will share their perspectives on macroeconomic trends, market performance and future growth opportunities.\n\nThe forum will highlight the resilience and potential of the market, showcasing recent policy reforms, improved infrastructure and a robust ecosystem that supports sustainable investment."
