    "chunk_size_bytes": 1215,
    "chunk_text": "The programme was handled by the specially created Bureau of the Commissioner General of Rehabilitation \u2013 the government can establish a similar structure for a mass drug rehabilitation initiative.\u00a0 It does not necessarily need to be headed by the military top brass,\u00a0 but the facilities, organisational competency, and fast expertise of the defence forces should be utilised within a civilian-led initiative. The rehabilitation of LTTE cadres lasted 12 to 18 months, and included mandatory counselling, post-traumatic stress therapy and vocational training of\u00a0 40 technical and vocational skills, including IT, carpentry, masonry, tailoring, plumbing and agriculture.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s prison crisis is an extension of a growing crisis in drug addiction. One cannot be addressed without the other.\u00a0 The president should revisit the success of the previous rehabilitation programme. That it was undertaken by the Rajapaksas or was foul-mouthed by NGO busybodies should not dissuade the president. He should call on the military expertise of the past, and facilities and manpower at the present. The clock is ticking. The trigger for the next mass protests may be in the overcrowded and ill-managed prison system."
