    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka has most favourable view of India globally\n\nColombo, August 15 (Daily Mirror) - Sri Lanka has the most favourable view of India, with 79% of adults expressing a positive opinion, according to a new survey by the Pew Research Center.\n\nThe survey, conducted across 36 countries between February and May 2026, found that views of India remain divided globally, with a median of 45% of respondents holding a favourable opinion and 41% expressing an unfavourable view.\n\nSri Lanka recorded the highest level of favourable sentiment towards India among the countries surveyed, reflecting the close historical, economic and cultural ties between the two neighbouring countries.\n\nThe survey also found significant differences in attitudes towards India across regions, with perceptions shaped by geopolitical developments, historical rivalries and evolving international relationships.\n\nIndia\u2019s immediate neighbourhood showed particularly contrasting views. In Pakistan, only 7% of adults expressed a favourable opinion of India, the lowest figure recorded in the survey.\n\nTurkey was another major outlier, with 15% expressing a favourable view, while only 18% of respondents in the West Bank and East Jerusalem viewed India positively.\n\nDespite these negative perceptions in some countries, India enjoys considerable goodwill in several parts of the world, including Western Europe and East Africa.\n\nThe findings come as India marks 79 years of independence and provide a snapshot of global public opinion towards the world\u2019s most populous country amid its growing economic and geopolitical influence."
