    "chunk_text": "Eleven rescued after fast attack craft runs into distress off Angulana\n\nColombo, August 15 (Daily Mirror) - Eleven crew members of a Sri Lanka Navy fast attack craft that encountered distress in the seas off Angulana have been rescued and admitted to hospital, while one person remains missing, Police said.\n\nThe incident occurred while the vessel was on a routine patrol in the area.\n\nFollowing the incident, a search and rescue operation was launched involving the Sri Lanka Navy, Sri Lanka Air Force, Police and local residents.\n\nThe rescued naval personnel were taken to hospital for medical evaluation.\n\nSearch operations are continuing to locate the missing crew member.\n\nFurther details regarding the circumstances surrounding the incident are yet to be confirmed."
