    "chunk_text": "Six people were wounded by strikes early Sunday, according to Ukrainian president Volodymyr Zelensky.\n\nKremenchuk and Kryvyi Rih in central Ukraine were also hit with ballistic missiles, Zelensky said. Two people were killed in Kryvyi Rih and another in Sumy in the north, Zelensky said.\n\nRussia fired more than 1,550 attack drones, nearly 1,560 guided aerial bombs and 62 missiles at Ukraine over the last week, according to Zelensky.\n\n\u201cEuropean interceptors cannot simply be allowed to sit in storage. Lives need to be protected. Russia must be stopped,\u201d he added.\n\nElsewhere, an unidentified drone was shot down Sunday in Romanian airspace, according to the Defense ministry in Bucharest. The drone was intercepted by a Spanish F-18 fighter jet pilot on a NATO air policing mission.\n\nIt was the fourth drone shot down this year over Romania, the defense ministry said.\n\nThe ministry said its radars detected the drone entering the country from neighboring Moldova. Fragments appeared to have fallen in an uninhabited area between two villages.\n\nIn July, Romanian F-16 fighter jet pilots shot down three Russian drones breaching national airspace for the first time after dozens of such incursions in the more than four years of Moscow\u2019s invasion of Ukraine."
