    "md5": "5d9adc22867c4609371c2acbc71e9324",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1763,
    "chunk_text": "Science College produce stunning rugby to lift U-16 Elite Ten-a-Side Cup\n\nAUG.16 (Mirror Sports) - Science College produced a superb display of running rugby to dethrone defending champions Wesley College 29-5 in the Cup final of the All Island Under-16 Elite Ten-a-Side Rugby Championship 2026, which concluded at the St. Peter\u2019s College ground in Bambalapitiya.\n\nThe achievement was particularly significant for Science College, who had finished runners-up to Wesley in 2025.\n\nScience impressed throughout the tournament with their attacking flair, ball movement, and commitment, culminating in a convincing victory over Wesley in the Cup final.\n\nMalindu Munasinghe of Science College was adjudged the Best Player of the Tournament after playing a key role in his team\u2019s outstanding campaign.\n\nIn the Cup semi-finals, Wesley College edged St. Anthony\u2019s College 14-12, while Science College produced an impressive 22-0 win over St. Peter\u2019s College to book their place in the final.\n\nThe three Kandy schools won three trophies, with Trinity College, Dharmaraja College, and Vidyartha College securing the Plate, Bowl, and Shield trophies respectively.\n\nTrinity defeated Royal College 12-5 in the Plate final, while Dharmaraja College clinched the Bowl with a hard-fought 14-12 victory over Isipathana College.\n\nVidyartha College completed a dominant Shield campaign, defeating Sri Piyarathne College 34-0 in the final.\n\nShield semi-finals: Sri Piyarathne beat Lumbini College 10-5, Vidyartha beat Mahanama 12-7\n\nBowl semi-finals: Isipathana beat Ananda 7-0, Dharmaraja beat Thurstan 28-5\n\nPlate semi-finals: Trinity beat D.S. Senanayake 7-0, Royal beat S. Thomas\u2019 10-0\n\nCup semi-finals: Wesley beat St. Anthony\u2019s 14-12, Science beat St. Peter\u2019s 22-0"
