    "chunk_size_bytes": 639,
    "chunk_text": "Govt will have to hold referendum or PC polls to survive: SJB\n\nColombo, Aug. 17 (Daily Mirror) - The government will have to hold some kind of election if to survive in a situation where its popularity is on the decline, Samagi Jana Balawegaya (SJB) MP Mujibur Rahman said today.\n\n\"The government will have to hold either a referendum to get the people's approval for the 22nd amendment or the Provincial Council elections which are pending. It is not possible to hold a general election or a Presidential poll,\" the MP told the media.\n\nHe was referring to the Verite Research report which claimed the government's popularity has declined."
