    "chunk_text": "Broader market participation remained weak, with only 75 securities advancing against 132 decliners, resulting in an advance-to-decline ratio of 0.57. The negative breadth indicated relatively widespread selling pressure despite gains among selected heavyweight counters.\n\nLion Brewery recorded the largest negative contribution, reducing the ASPI by 8.81 points. Richard Pieris, RIL Property, Colombo Dockyard and Citizens Development Business Finance also weighed on the index.\n\nAmong notable trades, Melstacorp recorded the highest individual counter turnover at LKR 599.10 million, followed by Dialog Axiata with LKR 93.22 million and Sampath Bank with LKR 81.54 million.\n\nOverall, the session reflected a divergence between broader market sentiment and large-cap performance. While the S&P SL20 continued to advance, weak market breadth, persistent foreign selling and the marginal decline in the ASPI indicated a more cautious start to the week."
