    "chunk_size_bytes": 1847,
    "chunk_text": "Dialog doubles 2Q profit to Rs.10.1bn as operating margins widen\n\nDialog Axiata PLC nearly doubled its group profit in the second quarter of 2026, as the revenue growth, wider operating margins and lower net finance costs strengthened the earnings.\n\nThe group profit attributable to the shareholders rose 99.6 percent to Rs.10.11 billion in the three months ended June 30, from Rs.5.07 billion a year earlier, according to the company\u2019s interim financial statements.\n\nThe quarterly revenue grew 9.3 percent to Rs.48.22 billion, from Rs.44.13 billion, supported by a growth in the data and home broadband revenue.\n\nThe direct costs were broadly unchanged at Rs.20.79 billion, despite the increase in revenue, lifting gross profit by 17.2 percent to Rs.27.43 billion. The gross profit margin improved to 56.9 percent, from 53.0 percent a year earlier.\n\nThe distribution and administrative expenses also declined marginally, helping the operating profit surge 45.7 percent to Rs.13.01 billion. Dialog\u2019s operating margin expanded to 27.0 percent, from 20.2 percent.\n\nThe bottom line received a further boost from the lower financing costs and a reversal in foreign-exchange movements. The net finance costs fell 45 percent to Rs.1.38 billion, from Rs.2.52 billion, as the group recorded a foreign-exchange gain of Rs.516 million, compared with a Rs.398 million loss in the corresponding quarter. Dialog said the earnings were \u201csupported by a strong EBITDA growth, lower net finance costs and foreign exchange gains, primarily arising from the timely execution of forward contracts against the future US dollar-denominated liabilities.\u201d\n\nExcluding the foreign-exchange gains, the underlying second-quarter profit after tax amounted to Rs.9.6 billion, up 76 percent from a year earlier and 4 percent from the preceding quarter, the company said."
  },
