    "md5": "0f83042695625a915e53b049bd650336",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1526,
    "chunk_text": "SLT group delivers 55% profit growth in second quarter\n\nSri Lanka Telecom PLC\u2019s (SLT) group profit rose 55 percent year-on-year (YoY) in the second quarter of 2026, supported by the higher revenue, stronger operating earnings and a sharp increase in foreign exchange gains.\n\nThe group profit attributable to the shareholders climbed to Rs.3.53 billion in the three months ended June 30, from Rs.2.27 billion a year earlier, according to the interim financial statements filed with the Colombo Stock Exchange.\n\nRevenue grew 12 percent to Rs.30.52 billion, while the direct costs rose at a slower 8 percent to Rs.15.46 billion. This lifted the gross profit by 15 percent to Rs.15.06 billion.\n\nThe operating profit advanced 30 percent to Rs.5.03 billion, despite the administrative expenses increasing 13 percent to Rs.6.91 billion. The sales and marketing costs were broadly unchanged at Rs.3.12 billion.\n\nThe quarterly earnings also received a sizeable boost from the foreign exchange gains, which surged to Rs.732 million, from Rs.52 million in the corresponding period. The finance costs declined 4 percent to Rs.1.73 billion, while the interest income increased 21 percent to Rs.389 million. However, other income recorded a negative Rs.83 million, compared with the income of Rs.510 million a year earlier, partly offsetting the improvement in the core operations and foreign exchange gains. Group profit before tax rose 48 percent to Rs.4.37 billion, while the income tax expenses increased 23 percent to Rs.838 million."
