    "md5": "458800d5ac99a28ec6ed0e0b7526a518",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1621,
    "chunk_text": "The NPP and economic democracy\n\nNeedless to say, none of these hapless parents and children are from affluent families\n\nThe brutal assault and abandonment of a four-year-old girl in Wattegama by her mother last week is part of a broader, recurring pattern of abuse rather than an isolated incident.\n\nAccording to reports, the mother of the child along with her paramour had brutally assaulted the girl at home, inflicted her with burn injuries with a lighter, and subjected her to repeated cruelty before abandoning her on a side road in Wattegama.\n\nDropping a child of only four years old in a place 36 kilometers away from her home, so that she could never find her way home shows the depth of the mother\u2019s cruel mindset. Such crimes against children are not limited to a particular area or a race or a religion and this is not the first of its kind. Also given the pattern of the incidents, this could also not be the last such incident.\n\nAnother mother in Weligama had left her one year old infant with her fourteen-year-old sister-in-law a few years ago under the pretext of visiting her husband and fled the area. In the same year, a disabled man had left his two sons aged four and five years at the Mahanama Bridge in Matara and had allegedly attempted to commit suicide by jumping into the Nilawala Ganga. According a similar report, two children were thrown into Kalu Ganga by their mother and were rescued by three army personnel on duty nearby.\n\nA sharp observer of child cruelty in the country would provide a long list of incidents of child abuse already published in the media, before they are forgotten."
