    "chunk_size_bytes": 706,
    "chunk_text": "Two arrested with deer antlers, elephant tusk ornaments in Kuruwita raid\n\nColombo, Aug. 18 (Daily Mirror) - Two persons in possession of animal body parts, including antlers, hides and ornaments made from elephant tusks, were arrested during a raid conducted by the Police Special Task Force (STF) in the Kuruwita area, the Department of Wildlife Conservation said.\n\nThe raid was carried out based on intelligence information provided by the Sri Lanka Air Force.\n\nInvestigators recovered three sambar deer antlers, four pairs of spotted deer antlers, the hide of a jackal and several ornaments carved from elephant tusks.\n\nThe animals concerned are protected under the Fauna and Flora Protection Ordinance."
