    "chunk_text": "Mundubile\u2019s National Reconciliation Party for Unity and Prosperity (NRPUP) rejected that account, saying the raid took place at their leader\u2019s home and left a member of parliament wounded by gunfire.\n\nMundubile said he had received information \u2060about the possible alteration of result forms from \u2060polling stations and called for an urgent independent investigation.\n\nInternational observers, including the European Union, said the election was largely peaceful, but that the \u201cbroader electoral process took place in an environment that limited fundamental freedoms\u201d.\n\n\u201cLate legal changes, legal uncertainty, and unequal campaign conditions distorted the playing field,\u201d said Michael McNamara, chief of the EU observation mission.\n\nZambia, home to 22 million people and Africa\u2019s second-largest copper producer, has a long record of peaceful transfers of power through the ballot box. Every change of president since the return to multiparty politics in 1991 has been achieved through elections."
