    "md5": "b8a83fd4b542c2259c9c8f98a7116072",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1920,
    "chunk_text": "Ukraine fires nearly 800 drones at Russia in one of war\u2019s biggest attacks\n\nINDIA TODAY - Ukraine launched one of its biggest drone attacks on Russia since Moscow\u2019s invasion more than four years ago, firing almost 800 drones overnight, officials said on Tuesday. The strike came just two days after a similar barrage, as both sides stepped up long-range attacks far from the front line.\n\nAt the same time, a Russian missile strike on Pechenihy village in Ukraine\u2019s north-eastern Kharkiv region killed 10 civilians, according to preliminary information from regional officials. President Volodymyr Zelenskyy described it as \"a brutal attack\", while officials said homes and civilian infrastructure were damaged.\n\nThe two countries are locked in an escalating duel of aerial strikes, with analysts saying there has been no major progress on the roughly 1,250-kilometre front line in eastern and southern Ukraine. Large numbers of drones and ground robots have restricted troop movement on both sides.\n\nOver the past year, Ukraine has developed and deployed domestically made long-range drones to strike deep inside Russia. Kyiv has said it wants Russians to feel the consequences of the war and to pressure President Vladimir Putin into peace talks. Putin, however, has shown no sign of stopping the invasion. Ukrainian Foreign Minister Andrii Sybiha said on X, \"Putin continues to drag out the war instead of accepting Ukraine\u2019s realistic ceasefire proposals and ending the bloodshed.\"\n\nRussia\u2019s Defence Ministry said air defences intercepted 791 Ukrainian drones over several Russian regions, as well as over annexed Crimea and the Black and Azov seas. According to an Associated Press tally, it was the second-largest drone attack since January 2025. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said more than 600 Ukrainian drones headed towards the Moscow region, where 180 were shot down, though he gave no further details."
