    "chunk_text": "Russia\u2019s Defence Ministry said air defences intercepted 791 Ukrainian drones over several Russian regions, as well as over annexed Crimea and the Black and Azov seas. According to an Associated Press tally, it was the second-largest drone attack since January 2025. Moscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin said more than 600 Ukrainian drones headed towards the Moscow region, where 180 were shot down, though he gave no further details.\n\nCoverage of the attack in Russian state and Kremlin-backed media was limited. Russia 1 and Channel One did not mention it in their morning bulletins. State news agency RIA Novosti, however, carried it among the main items on its website, calling it \"one of the most large-scale attacks on Moscow since the beginning of the summer\". State newspaper Rossiyskaya Gazeta highlighted Vorobyov\u2019s account of the attack and described it as \"massive\" in its headline, while pro-Kremlin tabloid MK carried a brief on its home page.\n\nIn Ukraine, Kharkiv regional military administration head Oleh Syniehubov said the missile strike on Pechenihy killed 10 civilians and wounded 17 others. Zelenskyy said, \"We will definitely respond to this Russian strike.\" Syniehubov said the attack damaged 10 homes, a cafe, a post office, a store and at least seven vehicles.\n\nElsewhere, Ukraine\u2019s National Police said three people were killed and three others wounded in Russian attacks on the Sumy region over the past day, including drone strikes and an explosive device blast."
