    "chunk_size_bytes": 1966,
    "chunk_text": "Parliament meets Gampaha youth to hear their ideas, concerns and policy proposals\n\nThe Parliamentary Caucus for Open Parliament Initiative and the Coalition for Inclusive Impact (CII) are working together to create these spaces for meaningful youth\u2013Parliament engagement, with the first phase providing a foundation for expanding the dialogue to additional districts in the future. The Gampaha engagement forms part of the first phase of a broader Voice to Policy Dialogue series covering Gampaha, Kandy and Batticaloa\n\nOver 65 young people engage with seven Members of Parliament at the first Voice to Policy Dialogue under a wider district-level youth\u2013Parliament engagement initiative\n\nOver 65 young people from Gampaha District came together with seven Members of Parliament at the Voice to Policy Dialogue on Sunday, creating a direct platform for Parliament to listen to the ideas, concerns and policy proposals of young people and discuss how these perspectives can contribute to future policy discussions.\n\nThe dialogue was organised by the Parliamentary Caucus for Open Parliament Initiative of the Parliament of Sri Lanka, in partnership with the Coalition for Inclusive Impact (CII), at the Jetwing Blue Hotel in Negombo.\n\nThe Gampaha dialogue is the first of three district-level engagements planned under the first phase of the Voice to Policy Dialogue initiative, with similar dialogues to be held with young people in Kandy and Batticaloa. The initiative is intended to create direct and structured opportunities for young people in different parts of the country to identify issues affecting their communities, develop policy proposals and engage directly with Members of Parliament. Following the first phase, similar engagements are envisaged in additional districts.\n\nThe Voice to Policy Dialogue puts the principles of the Open Parliament Initiative into practice by creating a structured space for citizens to engage directly with Parliament."
