    "md5": "74bac0c6bcd563adcf02ae982bf3e4c4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "The Gampaha dialogue is the first of three district-level engagements planned under the first phase of the Voice to Policy Dialogue initiative, with similar dialogues to be held with young people in Kandy and Batticaloa. The initiative is intended to create direct and structured opportunities for young people in different parts of the country to identify issues affecting their communities, develop policy proposals and engage directly with Members of Parliament. Following the first phase, similar engagements are envisaged in additional districts.\n\nThe Voice to Policy Dialogue puts the principles of the Open Parliament Initiative into practice by creating a structured space for citizens to engage directly with Parliament.\n\nThe program was designed around two stages. In the first stage, young participants worked together through a participatory process to identify concerns, explore different perspectives, cluster common issues and collectively prioritise areas requiring policy attention. Participants then developed recommendations and prepared their priority areas for presentation to Members of Parliament.\n\nThe second stage brought the youth representatives together with Members of Parliament for a direct dialogue. Youth representatives presented their priorities, followed by a structured discussion with parliamentarians and an open-floor session where participants could raise questions and concerns. The program concluded with a read-back of the recommendations and Members\u2019 responses.\n\nThe dialogue was attended by the Parliamentary Caucus for Open Parliament Initiative Co-Chairs Prof. Krishantha Abeysena MP and Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam MP, together with Chamindranee Kiriella MP, S.M. Marikkar MP, Prageeth Maduranga MP, Major General (Rtd.) G.D. Sooriyabandara MP, and Champika Hettiarachchi MP."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
