    "chunk_size_bytes": 1818,
    "chunk_text": "The dialogue was attended by the Parliamentary Caucus for Open Parliament Initiative Co-Chairs Prof. Krishantha Abeysena MP and Shanakiyan Rajaputhiran Rasamanickam MP, together with Chamindranee Kiriella MP, S.M. Marikkar MP, Prageeth Maduranga MP, Major General (Rtd.) G.D. Sooriyabandara MP, and Champika Hettiarachchi MP.\n\nThe discussions reflected the diverse concerns and aspirations of young people in Gampaha.\n\nParticipants raised issues relating to education and higher education, vocational training, employment and livelihoods, entrepreneurship, political participation, governance, healthcare, public infrastructure development, technology and digital transformation, cryptocurrency and emerging economic opportunities, among other areas.\n\nSpecific concerns and proposals included exploring ways to reduce the time required for young people to complete higher education and graduate, creating greater opportunities and pathways for young people interested in politics and public service, and improving awareness of and access to entrepreneurship opportunities.\n\nThe discussion also highlighted the importance of ensuring that young people are better equipped to benefit from emerging opportunities in technology, entrepreneurship and employment, while addressing wider public policy concerns relating to healthcare, infrastructure and governance.\n\nA key outcome of the dialogue was a commitment to take the recommendations and issues raised by young participants forward for consideration within Parliament.\n\nThe Parliamentary Caucus also indicated that relevant young people could be invited to engage with appropriate parliamentary committees, creating a pathway through which young people\u2019s knowledge, experiences and proposals can contribute to parliamentary deliberations beyond the dialogue itself."
