    "md5": "33f97493355cccca932b605e7131455a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 745,
    "chunk_text": "Man arrested over alleged LTTE camp hoax\n\nColombo, Aug. 19 (Daily Mirror) - A 46-year-old man has been arrested by the Terrorism Investigation Division (TID) for allegedly spreading false and unverified information claiming that an LTTE training camp was operating inside a forest reserve in Akkarayankulam.\n\nAccording to the Police, the suspect allegedly circulated the claims through a video on social media and during a media briefing.\n\nPolice said he was arrested on August 18 over allegations that an LTTE training camp was being operated in the Palai forest reserve within the Akkarayankulam Police area.\n\nHe is due to be produced before the Colombo Chief Magistrate\u2019s Court.\n\nGovt denies claims of LTTE training camp operating in Pallai"
  },
