    "chunk_size_bytes": 1935,
    "chunk_text": "Korean envoy visits Colombo Hyundai-Abans Auto flagship store\n\nAmbassador of the Republic of Korea Miyon Lee visited the Hyundai flagship store located at No. 65, Kirula Road, Colombo 5, underscoring the long-standing relationship between Sri Lanka and the Republic of Korea and the important role of trusted Korean partnerships in strengthening commercial and cultural ties between the two countries.\n\nThe visit provided an opportunity to celebrate Hyundai\u2019s presence in Sri Lanka through its partner Abans Auto and to recognise the enduring partnership fostered through the efforts of Abans Auto.\n\nAs one of Korea\u2019s most prominent and globally recognised automotive brands, Hyundai continues to represent Korean innovation, engineering and excellence on the international stage.\n\nDuring the visit, Lee toured the Hyundai flagship showroom and viewed the latest models showcased by Hyundai in Sri Lanka. Particular attention was given to Hyundai PALISADE, SANTA FE and VENUE, with Lee expressing her appreciation for the new models on display.\n\nShe was accompanied by Embassy of the Republic of Korea in Colombo Vice Consul Jung Haesung.\n\nRepresenting Abans Auto during the visit were Abans Auto Director Darius Pestonjee, Abans Auto General Manager Rajitha Ranasinghe, Abans Auto Senior Manager Shashika Rathnasekera, Abans Auto Senior Manager Deeves Clark, Abans Auto Product Manager Darren Stork, Abans Auto Assistant Sales Manager Maneka Dhanawardhana, Abans Auto Sales Executive Husni Ahmed and Abans Auto Sales Executive Isham Irshad.\n\nThe visit also highlighted the value placed on building lasting connections between Sri Lanka and Korea through trusted partnerships and the presence of internationally respected Korean brands in the Sri Lankan market.\n\nThe continued collaboration between Hyundai and Abans Auto reflects this relationship, with Abans Auto bringing Hyundai\u2019s global range closer to Sri Lankan consumers."
