    "md5": "0c623d8009ca628ad585821649d07011",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1735,
    "chunk_text": "CEAT ranked as SL\u2019s Most Valuable tyre brand\n\nCEAT Kelani Holdings, Brand Finance and Echelon Media senior management representatives at Most Valuable Tyre Brand 2026 plaque presentation\n\nAlso rated strongest tyre brand and 11th strongest brand in country overall across all sectors\n\nCEAT has reinforced its position at the forefront of Sri Lanka\u2019s automotive sector, being ranked as the Most Valuable tyre brand in the country, strongest tyre brand in the market and 11th strongest brand overall across all sectors in the 2026 edition of the Brand Finance \u2018Sri Lanka 100\u2019.\n\nThe latest report by Brand Finance, the world\u2019s leading brand valuation consultancy, values the CEAT brand at Rs.2,544 million as at January 1, 2026, marking a notable increase from Rs.2,325 million in 2025.\n\nIn terms of overall brand value, CEAT has advanced to the 43rd place among Sri Lanka\u2019s 100 most valuable brands, improving its position by one place year-on-year.\n\nCEAT\u2019s brand\u2019s Brand Strength Index (BSI) score of 80.3 out of 100 underpins its standing as the strongest tyre brand in the country, while its AAA- (Extremely Strong) Brand Strength Rating, unchanged from the previous year, places CEAT in the same league as some of Sri Lanka\u2019s most trusted household names.\n\nAccording to Brand Finance, CEAT continues to demonstrate a strong performance across key brand drivers, recording the highest scores for consideration and reputation, while also showing resilience in a challenging operating environment.\n\nOn the global stage, CEAT\u2019s credentials are further reinforced by its ranking as the fourth strongest tyre brand worldwide, with a BSI score of 84.9, highlighting the brand\u2019s competitiveness in international markets."
  },
