    "chunk_text": "ComBank partners SolarRay Energy to expand access to green financing\n\nW. D. Jayasuriya, Chief Manager of the Retail Products Department of Commercial Bank and Elabada Liyanage Chamil Suranga Silva, Managing Director of SolarRay Energy exchange the agreement\n\nDriven by its commitment to providing sustainable financial solutions for its customers, Commercial Bank of Ceylon has signed a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with SolarRay Energy (Pvt) Ltd. to promote the Bank\u2019s Green Loans and Green Leases, enabling employed and self-employed customers to access affordable financing for solar energy solutions.\n\nThe partnership was formalised at a signing ceremony attended by Chamil Suranga Silva and senior officials of SolarRay Energy (Pvt) Ltd., and W. D. Jayasuriya \u2013 Chief Manager of the Retail Products Department of Commercial Bank, along with senior officials of the Bank.\n\nUnder this partnership, customers of SolarRay Energy will be able to finance the purchase and installation of solar panels through Commercial Bank\u2019s Green Loans and Green Leases, offered at preferential interest rates with repayment periods of up to five years. The preferential rates and benefits under this promotion will be available until 3rd August 2027.\n\nThe initiative is part of Commercial Bank\u2019s ongoing efforts to promote environmentally responsible practices, expand its portfolio of green financing products, and encourage more customers to adopt sustainable energy solutions.\n\nSolarRay Energy will support customers with a comprehensive suite of services including engineering solutions at the interface between power assets and utility networks, feasibility studies, and Engineering, Procurement, and Construction Management (EPCM) advisory services, as well as operation and maintenance services to ensure optimal system performance."
  },
