    "chunk_text": "Financial details of the partnership and the investment associated with the two properties were not disclosed.\n\nAccor South Asia CEO Ranju Alex said Sri Lanka represented an important growth market for the hotel group, supported by demand across business, leisure and experiential tourism.\n\nSoftlogic Group Chairman and Managing Director Ashok Pathirage said the partnership reflected the group\u2019s longer-term confidence in Sri Lanka\u2019s economic recovery and tourism prospects.\n\nHe said the two hotels were expected to target business travellers, conferences, social events and leisure visitors while supporting employment and tourism-related economic activity.\n\nThe simultaneous launch strengthens Accor\u2019s presence in Sri Lanka while giving Softlogic exposure to an internationally established premium hotel brand. The properties will also participate in Accor\u2019s global booking and loyalty programme, ALL Accor.\n\nAccor India and South Asia currently operates 75 hotels spanning the luxury, premium, midscale and economy categories. Its regional portfolio includes brands such as Raffles, Fairmont, Sofitel, Pullman, Grand Mercure, Novotel, Mercure, ibis and ibis Styles.\n\nPullman operates more than 150 hotels globally. Accor\u2019s wider portfolio comprises over 5,700 properties across more than 110 countries."
