    "chunk_text": "\u201cThat\u2019s only part of the story about international capital. You see, international capital also forces governance,\u201d he explained. \u201cWith that capital comes knowledge anyway, and also remember international capital will help reduce interest rates domestically because of the liquidity that it brings. So for all of these reasons, I think it is important for us to think about what makes international capital conducive.\u201d\n\n\u201cFinally, I think we should be careful. While it\u2019s tempting for us to rubbish the public sector and to question the value of democracy, I think these are really dangerous things to say,\u201d Mannakkara emphasised. \u201cBecause democracy is the ultimate safety valve. Yes, it\u2019s messy, yes, it\u2019s annoying, but it\u2019s what gives us resilience.\u201d\n\nThe exchange underscored a deeper ideological divide within the business community regarding the optimal path forward for the economy, as policymakers and corporate leaders continue to grapple with balancing the demand for swift, unhindered reforms against the essential checks, balances, and global integrations required for long-term stability."
