    "md5": "4ab932adf51a9af1d5653f6d7cb4d69b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1496,
    "chunk_text": "Suthar six-fer seals India\u2019s 165-run win in Galle\n\nAUG.19 (Mirror Sports) - India sealed a 165-run victory over Sri Lanka in the first Test at Galle, taking a 1-0 lead in the two-match series despite a brave fight from Sonal Dinusha.\n\nChasing 372 for victory, Sri Lanka were bowled out for 206, with Dinusha once again leading the resistance. The left-hander followed his first-innings century with a determined 84, but found little support as India closed out the match.\n\nManav Suthar was the key figure for India, finishing with 6 for 55 to break Sri Lanka\u2019s lower-order resistance and complete the victory.\n\nSri Lanka had earlier been set a daunting target after India made 462 in the first innings and added 193 in their second. Devdutt Padikkal\u2019s 167 and KL Rahul\u2019s 82 formed the backbone of India\u2019s first-innings total.\n\nSri Lanka responded with 284, with Dinusha making a century, but India retained a 178-run lead before setting up the fourth-innings chase.\n\nDhananjaya de Silva added 59 in Sri Lanka\u2019s final innings, but the hosts could not build enough partnerships around Dinusha to keep the chase alive.\n\nOnce Dinusha departed for 84, Sri Lanka\u2019s resistance quickly faded, allowing India to secure victory and move ahead in the series.\n\nThe second and final Test will be played at the SSC in Colombo from August 23 to 27, with Sri Lanka needing a win to level the series.\n\nFor Sri Lanka, Dinusha\u2019s century and 84 were the biggest positives from a disappointing result."
  },
