    "chunk_text": "Market breadth nevertheless remained negative, with 72 securities advancing against 128 decliners, resulting in an advance-to-decline ratio of 0.56. This indicated that selling pressure remained relatively broad despite the return of foreign buying.\n\nSampath Bank recorded the largest negative contribution, reducing the ASPI by 17.68 points. Lion Brewery, Central Finance, Bukit Darah and Dialog Axiata also weighed on the index.\n\nAmong notable trades, Sunshine Holdings recorded the highest individual counter turnover at LKR 220.61 million, followed by Seylan Bank with LKR 200.22 million and Dialog Axiata with LKR 163.07 million.\n\nOverall, the session reflected continued near-term weakness following the previous day\u2019s sharp decline. While the return of foreign buying was encouraging, negative market breadth and continued pressure on both benchmark indices indicated that broader investor sentiment remained cautious."
