    "chunk_text": "Demolition of Ahangama beachfront businesses makes no sense: SJB\n\nColombo, Aug. 19 (Daily Mirror) - SJB National Youth Organizer Chamith Wijesundera has criticised the demolition of beachfront businesses in Ahangama, saying the move makes little sense while Sri Lanka\u2019s economy remains fragile.\n\nIn a post on X, Wijesundera said tourism is one of the country\u2019s main sources of foreign exchange and employment, and urged the Government to focus on economic recovery, investment and job creation.\n\n\u201cDemolishing Ahangama beachfront businesses is the last thing Sri Lanka needs right now. Tourism is one of our main sources of Dollars and jobs. Destroying these spots when the economy is still fragile makes no sense,\u201d he said.\n\nHe called on the Government to focus on what he described as the country\u2019s real priorities \u2014 recovery, investment and jobs."
