    "chunk_size_bytes": 1865,
    "chunk_text": "ASUS launches AI-powered flagship ExpertBook Ultra in Sri Lanka\n\nFrom left:\u00a0 ASUS Vice President Commercial PC Sri Lanka, India and Nepal Dinesh Sharma, ASUS System Business Group APAC Commercial General Manager Vice President Rex Lee, and ASUS Sri Lanka Country Product Manager Medanka Mapalagama \u2013 Pic by Daminda Harsha Perera\n\nASUS has announced the Sri Lanka launch of the ASUS ExpertBook Ultra, the absolute industry flagship and a Copilot+ PC designed to enable CXOs and business leaders to achieve an ultra-state of mind where brilliance is born.\n\nIt features ultra-light design, elite cutting-edge AI-powered performance, vivid display, immersive audio, all day battery, ultimate typing experience, segment leading military grade durability, enterprise-grade security, super premium enterprise grade service support, and seamless expandability.\n\nThe ExpertBook portfolio is also expanded with B series (B3 and B5 models) and P series (P5 and P3 models) for high-performance AI productivity and future-proof scalability to meet the dynamic demands of enterprises and businesses across Sri Lanka. Powered by next-generation Intel Core Ultra Series 3 processor and AI-driven productivity, the new ExpertBook Ultra, B and P series business laptops are unified by the ASUS \u2018Worry-Free Business Experience\u2019 commitment, blending elite performance, enterprise security, military-grade durability, comprehensive connectivity and mobility, with Sri Lanka\u2019s most comprehensive commercial support ecosystem.\n\nThe ASUS ExpertBook Ultra is ultra-portable flagship meticulously crafted from AZ31B magnesium-aluminum alloy, a material typically reserved for Aerospace and Formula 1 applications, with a Nano Ceramic surface with a 9H hardness rating. It is engineered to deliver an unprecedented balance of performance, durability, aesthetics, and user experience."
