    "chunk_text": "\u201cThis is not just promises made in the air; it is very much solid, very much structured, very much planned,\u201d Hewawasam said while Deputy Minister of Tourism Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe reinforced the milestone, noting that \u201cthis has been a day that all were waiting for years.\u201d\n\n\u201cWhenever we sit for a press conference, the question that is asked is, \u2018Where is the global campaign?\u2019 So it is right here now, and we are launching it here today,\u201d he said.\n\nLooking ahead, the launch of the subsequent global campaign is designed to propel arrivals past the 3 million mark in 2027, yielding over 5 billion US dollars in earnings. Ultimately, this framework builds toward a long-term vision of 5 million arrivals and an annual revenue contribution of 8 billion to 10 billion US dollars by 2030. The core objective, however, extends far beyond headline volume. The primary structural challenge confronting the industry has long been the imbalance between volume and yield. As articulated during the launch, the central priority is attracting quality, high-spending visitors whose daily expenditure and dwell time reflect the true value of the island\u2019s offering, shifting the marketing narrative away from generic destination postcards toward high-yield, experiential engagements."
