    "chunk_size_bytes": 1973,
    "chunk_text": "The execution timeline presented by the SLTPB has been structured to maintain year-round international engagement, avoiding the fragmented, short-burst advertising attempts of the past. The Rs. 1.5 billion interim phase focuses on six primary source markets, beginning immediately in Australia with a six-month digital blitz and public relations campaign running from August 2026 to February 2027.\n\nMeanwhile, India will be engaged with a high-frequency, programmatic digital activation starting in October 2026 and running for seven months to capture tech-savvy, weekend-break, and wedding travelers. By April 2027, the digital and public relations machinery will expand into a wider secondary tier of high-value markets, establishing footprints in France, Italy, Spain, the Middle East, the Scandinavian nations, the Benelux region, Poland, Japan, and South Korea. Operating on a dedicated Rs. 5 billion budget, the full-scale global branding campaign will launch in March 2027 following Cabinet clearance and international procurement tenders, deploying a rolling 24-month master brand identity across international broadcast networks, global transit hubs, and digital platforms through February 2029.\n\nTo demonstrate the quantitative rigor underpinning the campaign, the presentation highlighted the specific key performance indicators established for the phase one Australia activation. The projected volume and engagement scope target 16 million to 18 million total ad impressions across all channels. The campaign aims for a combined reach of 5 million to 8 million individuals across YouTube, Meta, and TikTok, alongside driving 125,000 to 205,000 web traffic clicks directly to the campaign microsite and securing 4 million to 5 million full video content views. These performance benchmarks establish an operational discipline where every promotional rupee is tied directly to measurable reach, engagement, and referral traffic into destination booking platforms."
