    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b6856a3e90be3ac9121a1e3caa8a6eda",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1827,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market pitches investment case in Australia\n\nFrom left: Thulci Aluwihare - Deputy Managing Director at CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd; Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena - Director General of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka; Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara - Chairman of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka; Chathuranga Abeysinghe - Deputy Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development of Sri Lanka; Dr. P. Nandalal Weerasinghe - Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka; Dr. Naveen Gunawardane, Co-Founder and Managing Director of the Lynear Wealth Management (Pvt) Ltd; Damith Pallewatte -\u00a0 Managing Director / Chief Executive Officer of the Hatton National Bank PLC;\u00a0 Ray Abeywardena - Director of the Colombo Stock Exchange and Moderator Rajeeva Bandaranaike - Chief Executive Officer, Colombo Stock Exchange\n\nThe Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC) and the Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), in collaboration with Port City Colombo and the Sri Lanka High Commission in Australia, successfully hosted an \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 Investor Forum on 17 August at the Sheraton Grand Sydney Hyde Park.\n\nHNB Group served as the Platinum Partner, with the Australia Sri Lanka Business Council, Nalanda College Old Boys\u2019 Association Australia, and CA Sri Lanka Australia Chapter supporting the forum as Supporting Partners.\n\nThe forum was aimed at strengthening international investor confidence in Sri Lanka, promoting investment opportunities in the country\u2019s capital market, and facilitating greater participation by foreign fund managers and the Sri Lankan diaspora in Australia. The forum provided an opportunity to communicate these developments directly to international investors and highlight the opportunities emerging within Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market."
  },
