    "chunk_size_bytes": 1529,
    "chunk_text": "The forum was aimed at strengthening international investor confidence in Sri Lanka, promoting investment opportunities in the country\u2019s capital market, and facilitating greater participation by foreign fund managers and the Sri Lankan diaspora in Australia. The forum provided an opportunity to communicate these developments directly to international investors and highlight the opportunities emerging within Sri Lanka\u2019s capital market.\n\nIn his opening remarks, Ray Abeywardena, Director of the Colombo Stock Exchange stated, \u201cPolitical stability and strict discipline on the monetary side are two very key components that investors would look at when investing into a market.There will be a reallocation of funds into the frontier markets. And we are confident that Sri Lanka will be in a good position to attract a good amount of funds to be reinvested and reallocated into the frontier markets.\u201d\n\nEmphasising the role of the capital market in supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic transformation, Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, Chairman of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka, pointed out, \u201cSri Lanka is moving towards a path of inclusive and sustainable growth, but achieving higher growth will require investment and capital formation. Our capital market has a vital role to play in mobilising capital and supporting the next phase of Sri Lanka\u2019s economic growth. Through the Invest Sri Lanka Forums, we invite the Sri Lankan diaspora and international investors to be part of this journey.\u201d"
  },
