    "chunk_size_bytes": 1273,
    "chunk_text": "Emphasising the role of the capital market in supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s economic transformation, Senior Prof. D.B.P.H. Dissabandara, Chairman of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka, pointed out, \u201cSri Lanka is moving towards a path of inclusive and sustainable growth, but achieving higher growth will require investment and capital formation. Our capital market has a vital role to play in mobilising capital and supporting the next phase of Sri Lanka\u2019s economic growth. Through the Invest Sri Lanka Forums, we invite the Sri Lankan diaspora and international investors to be part of this journey.\u201d\n\nDr. Nandalal Weerasinghe, Governor of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, highlighted Sri Lanka\u2019s improving credit profile and the potential for further upgrades, \u201cThe IMF views Sri Lanka as a case study of a country that has achieved a relatively rapid recovery. With all three major international rating agencies currently rating Sri Lanka at CCC, there is a clear pathway towards an upgrade to B-, a level comparable to where we stood before the crisis. This reflects the improving confidence in Sri Lanka. Investors who wait for the ratings upgrade may find that the market has already priced in the improvement. The opportunity to invest is now\u201d."
