    "chunk_size_bytes": 1616,
    "chunk_text": "The forum also highlighted the opportunities available through Port City Colombo, particularly for international investors seeking greater flexibility in capital flows and access to overseas markets. Thulci Aluwihare, Deputy Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd, highlighted these opportunities, \u201cYou can invest in Australian dollars in Port City Colombo. Some of the restrictive repatriation and capital account rules that apply across South Asia do not apply in the Port City. The capital account is more relaxed because you are bringing your business capital from overseas, and your source markets and revenues are also overseas. That creates a much more flexible environment for international investors.\u201d\n\nThe forum concluded with an engaging panel discussion featuring the speakers and Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena, Director General of the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka, and moderated by Mr. Rajeeva Bandaranaike, Chief Executive Officer of the Colombo Stock Exchange. The discussion provided an opportunity for participants to engage with the panelists on Sri Lanka\u2019s economic outlook, capital market developments, investment opportunities and the country\u2019s positioning within the broader South Asian growth story.\n\nThe Sydney forum was the first of a series of \u201cInvest Sri Lanka\u201d Investor Forums being held in Australia from 17\u201320 August, bringing together policymakers, regulators, market professionals and investment industry representatives to showcase Sri Lanka\u2019s evolving investment landscape and engage directly with international investors and the Sri Lankan diaspora."
  },
