    "md5": "2561fd5068771ae91867fe7474766d7a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1835,
    "chunk_text": "JAT Holdings 1Q profit stalls despite 34% revenue growth\n\nJAT Holdings PLC recorded group revenue of Rs.3.04 billion for the quarter ended June 30, 2026, representing a 34 percent year-on-year increase, supported by growth across both its Sri Lankan and international operations.\n\nLocal revenue increased by 8 percent to Rs.1.83 billion, while revenue from the foreign operations increased by 110 percent to Rs.1.21 billion.\n\nGross profit increased by 29 percent to Rs.1.07 billion, while the gross profit margin moderated from 37 percent to 35 percent, reflecting the higher input costs associated with the increases in the global commodity prices.\n\nThe operating profit declined by 25 percent to Rs.174 million, primarily reflecting the consolidation of Mirotone\u2019s expenses, alongside the higher administrative, selling and distribution expenses associated with the Volt software depreciation, increased transportation costs, following the fuel price increases and additional warehouse capacity established to support wider market reach.\n\nThe foreign exchange gains partly offset the finance costs, with profit before tax remaining broadly unchanged at Rs.167 million and profit after tax at Rs.150 million.\n\nThe wood coatings business maintained its 57 percent market share while achieving an 8 percent quarter-on-quarter (QoQ) revenue growth, despite the supplier price increases that reduced the net gross profit margin by 4 percent. The paint, chemicals and related products segment recorded an 85 percent QoQ revenue growth, with its share of the Brilliant White segment increasing to 11 percent.\n\nBrushes and rollers delivered a 78 percent QoQ revenue growth, expanded its outlet reach by 12 percent to more than 3,000 outlets and further strengthened its market-leading position through a 3 percent increase in market share."
  },
