    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-main/SL-kicks-off-long-awaited-Rs-1-5bn-interim-campaign/245-348487",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787203314.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-20-dailymirrorlk-97d935c1-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "793bdc87a419c3c126c642c3d25e01e0",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1738,
    "chunk_text": "SL kicks off long-awaited Rs.1.5bn interim campaign\n\nImmediate Rs.1.5bn interim promotional drive paves way for a broader Rs.5bn global branding campaign in March 2027\n\nAuthorities revise 2026 projections upward, targeting 2.7mn tourist arrivals and US $ 4.2bn in earnings\n\nInterim campaign will be launched systematically across 6 primary source markets with market-specific strategies\n\nPrivate sector leaders urge strict accountability, monthly progress tracking and expanded joint mechanisms with international travel distributors\n\nThe Sri Lanka Tourism Promotion Bureau (SLTPB) yesterday officially launched a Rs.1.5 billion interim digital and public relations campaign, marking the country\u2019s first major structured international promotional push in over a decade.\n\nThe interim campaign will run from August 2026 through April 2027, specifically targeting six high-yielding source markets.\n\nThe launch is designed to capitalise on the upcoming winter booking season and restore Sri Lanka\u2019s destination visibility ahead of a broader Rs.5 billion global branding campaign scheduled to roll out in March 2027.\n\nThe authorities announced an upward revision of the country\u2019s tourism targets for the year, largely buoyed by the anticipated boost from this campaign. While the government previously downgraded its 2026 expectations to 2.5 million arrivals and US $ 3.5 billion in earnings, amidst the Middle East crisis and aviation disruptions, the targets have now been elevated.\n\nSLTPB Chairman Buddhika Hewawasam announced in Colombo yesterday that aided by the interim campaign and increased airline connectivity, the tourism authority now projects over 2.7 million arrivals and US $ 4.2 billion in earnings for the current year."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
