    "date_str": "2026-08-20",
    "description": "SL kicks off long-awaited Rs.1.5bn interim campaign",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-main/SL-kicks-off-long-awaited-Rs-1-5bn-interim-campaign/245-348487",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787203314.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-20-dailymirrorlk-97d935c1-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "55571647efa64453f7e35d11a1a6f9d3",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2008,
    "chunk_text": "SLTPB Chairman Buddhika Hewawasam announced in Colombo yesterday that aided by the interim campaign and increased airline connectivity, the tourism authority now projects over 2.7 million arrivals and US $ 4.2 billion in earnings for the current year.\n\nThe interim campaign will be launched systematically across six primary source markets, with market-specific strategies. In Australia, the campaign commences this August for a six-month period, featuring digital activations across platforms such as Meta, TikTok and YouTube, supplemented by roadshows in Melbourne, Sydney, Perth and Adelaide as well as Auckland and Christchurch in New Zealand.\n\nThe United Kingdom and Germany campaigns will kick off in September for an eight-month duration, strategically timed alongside the major industry events such as the World Travel Market in London and ITB Berlin.\n\nRead \u2018Inside Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic blueprint for global tourism marketing promo\u2019 on Page 13 for more detailsThe initiative will expand to China in September for a seven-month period to capture secondary cities, followed by India in October, with heavy digital activations targeting the tech-savvy travellers and OTA platforms.\n\nFurthermore, a focused winter seasonal campaign will run in Russia through March 2027.\n\nTourism Deputy Minister Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe emphasised that the promotional drive aims to attract the high-spending tourists and shift the focus toward specialised market segments such as wellness, diving and golf.\n\nHe noted that the global campaign, which has been delayed for a considerable period, will run through February 2029 and will be supported by an AI-powered travel discovery platform to optimise Sri Lanka\u2019s presence in global search engines.\n\n\u201cThis has been a day that all of us were waiting for years,\u201d Prof. Ranasinghe noted.\n\n\u201cWhenever we sit for a press conference, the question that is asked is, \u2018Where is the global campaign?\u2019 So, it is right here now and we are launching it here today.\u201d"
  },
  {
