    "chunk_index": 3,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "356420e6191ed88d87a0f2910a1a8d6e",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1676,
    "chunk_text": "Q\u00a0 AKD has moved from revolutionary leftist politics to leading a government that works within the existing state, market and international financial system. Do you believe he has betrayed the principles of the Left, or has he simply recognised that those principles cannot govern a modern state in their traditional form?\n\nThe JVP is not only a name, but also a brand. What Mr. Gotabhaya Rajapakse failed, by using AKD the JVP and the brand, which was created by the sacrifice of a number of comrades in the past, it\u2019s being invested into the neoliberal programme. So the United States of America, or India, or the IMF, the imperialist institutions are content with what is happening in Sri Lanka.\n\nQ\u00a0 You have historically opposed multinational corporations, global finance capital and institutions such as the IMF. But Sri Lanka\u2019s current economic reality is very different from the period when you entered politics. If you were responsible for governing the country today, how would you finance the economy, manage our debts and attract foreign investment without relying on the very institutions and capital you have criticised?\n\nI want to raise one question. What is the country which was successful by using this IMF programme or the IMF conditions? Look and countries like Greece and Argentina. Even the other countries where IMF programme was implemented it was a failure. In one hand, we have that reality, because this is not the first time, it\u2019s the 17th time.\n\nAccording to the Central Bank Governor we are short of dollars, and according to his explanation 8.2 billion US dollars is enough to pay debts. We are not going to gain that within a few months."
  },
