    "chunk_id": "2026-08-20-dailymirrorlk-6524264d-0005",
    "chunk_index": 5,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "394f26fa04a3223e04657077a289c622",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1960,
    "chunk_text": "Q\u00a0Don\u2019t you think that itself could create a monopoly where capitalists will get together and they will find a way to oppress the rest of the masses? When you try to impose tax on these people, don\u2019t you think that the downtrodden masses who work under them will be affected?\n\nOnce we try to accumulate, taxes from the top capitalists, they will attempt to topple the government. That\u2019s what I\u2019m saying, not only by the votes, but with the organizational power of the masses, we will come together. That is the way we are going to handle office. Whatever the actions we take and the attempts to implement, we should get the support from the masses, and they are active partners of this causes. That is the difference between us and other parties.\n\nQ\u00a0 The NPP has now occupied much of the political space traditionally associated with the Left, while the FSP remains outside Parliament. Has the NPP effectively made the FSP politically irrelevant or has the FSP failed to adapt to changing political realities?\n\nYes, I can give you one example. The JVP came in to power after 60 years. Until then, they maintained 3% of the votes. Therefore we don\u2019t worry about our voter base because we know that when the time comes and the situation arises, there will be change. No one expected the aragalaya (Protest) and the birth of the NPP government. The traditional parties which are in the opposition criticise the NPP government with regard to the ongoing issue with judges. The people no longer believe in them due to their past conduct. Whenever they raise an argument against the NPP government regarding this Chief Justice issue they revert to question about the appointment of Justice Shirani Bandaranaike.\n\nThis is why our stand is stronger and it affects the government. Throughout the history we were in the JVP. While we were there we expected a socialist society, and now they have changed all their policies get into action in a pragmatic way."
  },
