    "chunk_text": "I said pragmatism. Being pragmatic is good. But pragmatism is not good because, then you fall into the circumstances. You don\u2019t have a strategy. You don\u2019t have a plan, long term plan. Whatever the situation arises, you fall into that. So that is called pragmatism. Then you don\u2019t have a clear vision. The word Pragmatic is good because according to the situation, even though you have a plan and a vision and a strategic programme, still, you have to be practical. So that is a different thing. Pragmatism is totally different. You don\u2019t have a vision.\n\nQ\u00a0Would you support an alliance formed by the opposition parties if the objective is to defeat the NPP led government? If not, why?\n\nBut the reason why we, try to implement our programme by ourselves, doesn\u2019t mean we don\u2019t have any other. It is because there\u2019s no party or type of a group that we can deal with. We have experience with the parties which were in power and now with the NPP. Even though they are criticising each other in terms of policy and democracy, they are following the same path. Therefore, we should find a different path. We should follow our own path, and we should organise people, mobilise people, towards a progressive society."
