    "md5": "30dbff9b040fe32276842e601d250c79",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1910,
    "chunk_text": "New preschool guides launched under education reforms\n\nA set of new teacher and activity guides aimed at strengthening inquiry-based and activity-based learning in preschools has been launched under the Government\u2019s new education reform programme.\n\nThe Early Childhood Support Resource Guide, prepared in line with the Early Childhood Education Curriculum Framework, was launched recently at the Ministry of Education premises in Isurupaya under the patronage of Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya.\n\nThe initiative seeks to ensure that children receive quality education from the early stages of life by guiding preschool teachers towards a child-centred, play-based and inquiry-based approach to learning.\n\nThe resource package, prepared under the theme \u201cStarting Right\u201d, consists of four main components: the Teacher Guide, Suggested Activity Guide, Teaching and Learning Material Manual and Master Material Training Manual.\n\nThe guides are designed to provide preschool teachers, trainers and other stakeholders with practical guidance on introducing activity-based learning through play and other age-appropriate learning tools.\n\nThe programme is expected to be implemented across preschools islandwide, with training programmes for trainers and preschool teachers to be conducted throughout the country.\n\nThe initiative is being implemented under the leadership of the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education and the Ministry of Women and Child Affairs, with support from institutions including the National Institute of Education and UNICEF.\n\nThe Prime Minister said plans had been made to successfully introduce the new education reforms beginning with early childhood education.\n\nShe said the new guidelines represented a significant change in the learning process by promoting a child-centred, inquiry-based and activity-based approach to early childhood development."
  },
