    "chunk_size_bytes": 1373,
    "chunk_text": "The Prime Minister said plans had been made to successfully introduce the new education reforms beginning with early childhood education.\n\nShe said the new guidelines represented a significant change in the learning process by promoting a child-centred, inquiry-based and activity-based approach to early childhood development.\n\nThe Prime Minister also stressed the importance of educating parents on early childhood development and creating a society that is sensitive to children's needs and safety.\n\nMinister of Women and Child Affairs Saroja Savitri Paulraj said the guidelines represented a strong foundation for the country\u2019s future generations.\n\nShe said the Government expected to establish an islandwide preschool system operating under a single national policy by 2027, allowing parents to send their children to preschools with confidence.\n\nDeputy Minister of Women and Child Affairs Dr. Namal Sudarshana, Secretary to the Ministry of Education, Higher Education and Vocational Education Nalaka Kaluwewa, Director General of the National Institute of Education Senior Professor O. G. Dayaratne Banda, Additional Secretaries, provincial education authorities and UNICEF representatives were among those present at the event.\n\nThe guidelines can also be downloaded online through the official website of the National Institute of Education.\u00a0Pix by K.N.B. Herath"
