    "md5": "d0d4b9e82d96815269dabd43a884b8ba",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1068,
    "chunk_text": "Tipper-tractor crash claims five lives in Monaragala\n\nMonaragala, August 21 (Daily Mirror) - Five people have died following a serious road accident in the Kumbukkan area of Monaragala early this morning (21), police said.\n\nThe accident occurred on the Kalu Bridge along the Wellawaya\u2013Monaragala road when a tipper truck travelling towards Wellawaya collided with a tractor travelling in the opposite direction.\n\nAccording to police, 10 people were travelling on the tractor trailer at the time of the collision. Eight people sustained serious injuries and were rushed to the Monaragala Hospital for treatment.\n\nFive of the injured victims later succumbed to their injuries while receiving treatment at the hospital. The deceased were residents of Dodamgaslanda, Buttala, and Horabokka, and were aged 21, 26, 31, 55, and 56.\n\nThe remaining three injured individuals are currently receiving inpatient treatment at the Monaragala Hospital.\n\nBoth the driver of the tipper truck and the tractor driver have been taken into police custody in connection with the accident."
  },
