    "chunk_text": "Nanaska appoints Aubrey Joachim to board\n\nNanaska Executive Director Channa Gunawardena with former CIMA Global President Aubrey Joachim\n\nFormer CIMA Global President Aubrey Joachim joins Nanaska to shape future leaders\n\nNanaska, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s professional education institutes specialising in the Chartered Institute of Management Accountants (CIMA) qualification, announced the appointment of Aubrey Joachim, FCMA, CGMA, MBA, to its board as a Non-Executive Director.\n\nJoachim brings extensive international experience across finance leadership, consulting, professional development and finance function transformation.\n\nA former Global President of CIMA, Joachim held the position from 2009 to 2010, becoming the first person from outside the United Kingdom and Ireland to lead CIMA in its then 90-year history.\n\nOver a career spanning more than three decades, Joachim has held senior finance roles and worked with organisations and finance professionals across multiple international markets.\n\nHis experience has given him a strong understanding of how the finance function is evolving beyond the traditional reporting and control to play a more strategic role in business decision-making and value creation.\n\nThrough his consulting and professional development work, Joachim has been closely involved in areas including finance transformation, strategic management accounting, business partnering, forecasting, data and analytics and the development of future finance leaders.\n\nHe has also been an active voice on the impact of technological change on the profession, addressing developments in artificial intelligence (AI), automation, analytics and digital disruption and the new capabilities these require from finance professionals and business leaders."
