    "chunk_size_bytes": 765,
    "chunk_text": "Parliament pays tribute to late singer Nanda Malini\n\nParliament today paid tribute to late veteran singer Nanda Malini, recalling her immense contribution to Sri Lankan music and society.\n\nPrime Minister Harini Amarasuriya said the late singer was close to the hearts of all Sri Lankans and that her artistic works reflected the lives and experiences of the Sri Lankan people.\n\n\u201cHer voice was the voice of Sri Lankan society,\u201d the Prime Minister said.\n\nOpposition Leader Sajith Premadasa said he had known Nanda Malini since his childhood and recalled her strong connection with the people.\n\n\u201cShe stood with the people. She never deviated from her political stand,\u201d he said.\n\nParliament also observed a two-minute silence in her memory as a mark of respect."
