    "md5": "6ca8c804935b6c1f250855b90a7c66ea",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1781,
    "chunk_text": "Gazette notification on deploying elephants for Peraheras soon\n\nColombo, August 21 (Daily Mirror) - The Environment Ministry is preparing to issue a Gazette notification establishing a mechanism to regulate and deploy captive elephants for Peraheras and other cultural and religious events, following Cabinet approval for the initiative.\n\nThe move is aimed at strengthening governance, accountability and transparency in the management of captive elephants while ensuring compliance with Sri Lanka\u2019s national laws and international obligations, the Ministry said.\n\nThe initiative follows a comprehensive review of the legal and administrative framework governing the registration and management of captive elephants, changes in conservation priorities, law enforcement challenges, requirements for deploying elephants at cultural and religious events and animal welfare concerns.\n\nA special committee has been appointed by the Secretary to the Ministry of Environment to conduct a comprehensive study of these matters, obtain views from relevant stakeholders and review the draft \u201cRegistration and Licensing of Elephants Regulations 2026\u201d prepared by the Department of Wildlife Conservation.\n\nThe committee has also been tasked with submitting recommendations on a mechanism for deploying captive elephants for cultural and religious purposes, with particular attention to their welfare.\n\nThe committee is chaired by H.M.B.P. Herath, Additional Secretary (Policy, Legal Reforms and Parliamentary Affairs) of the Ministry of Environment, while D.P.C. Udaya Kumara, Additional Secretary (Development) of the Ministry, serves as its Convener and Secretary.\n\nThe committee is expected to submit its recommendations on the allocation of elephants for Peraheras in the near future."
  },
