    "md5": "7edc6ac147f6d40918590d593df7c0c6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1575,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka Expo 2027 promotional event in Melbourne highlights investment and trade opportunities\n\nThe Consulate General of Sri Lanka in Melbourne organised a \u201cSri Lanka Expo 2027\u201d promotional event on 14 August at the Consulate, bringing together Australian and Sri Lankan business stakeholders to explore trade, investment and business opportunities in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe event was attended by Export Development Board Chairman Mangala Wijesinghe and Board of Investment of Sri Lanka Director General Dr. Sulakshana Jayawardena.\n\nThe program provided Victoria-based business leaders and importers with first-hand information on investment opportunities, export potential and incentives available to international investors in Sri Lanka.\n\nVictoria-based companies interested in participating in Sri Lanka Expo 2027 attended the program, representing sectors including food and beverage, logistics, financial services, tourism and wellness. Victoria-based importers of leading Sri Lankan food and beverage brands also participated, providing an opportunity to discuss challenges affecting bilateral trade between Sri Lanka and Australia.\n\nAddressing the participants, Consul General, Pradeepa Saram highlighted Sri Lanka Expo 2027, to be held at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH), Colombo, from 14\u201317 January 2027, as one of the country\u2019s largest international business events and invited Australian and Sri Lankan business entities to use the Expo as a platform to establish new partnerships and explore business opportunities in Sri Lanka."
