    "chunk_size_bytes": 1449,
    "chunk_text": "Addressing the participants, Consul General, Pradeepa Saram highlighted Sri Lanka Expo 2027, to be held at the Bandaranaike Memorial International Conference Hall (BMICH), Colombo, from 14\u201317 January 2027, as one of the country\u2019s largest international business events and invited Australian and Sri Lankan business entities to use the Expo as a platform to establish new partnerships and explore business opportunities in Sri Lanka.\n\nBOI Director General Dr. Jayawardena briefed participants on investment opportunities in Sri Lanka, particularly in the industry, energy and mineral sectors, and explained the investor-friendly packages, incentives and other benefits available to foreign investors seeking to establish or expand operations in Sri Lanka. He further highlighted the new digital investment platform launched by the BOI to facilitate and attract foreign investment.\n\nThe discussion also focused on practical challenges faced by Victoria-based importers of Sri Lankan products, particularly lengthy procedures for obtaining Plant Quarantine and phytosanitary certification.\n\nIn response, EDB Chairman Wijesinghe assured participants that a meeting would be convened with the relevant agencies to identify solutions and streamline the process.\n\nThe promotional event underscored the Consulate General\u2019s continued efforts to strengthen Sri Lanka\u2013Australia trade and investment relations and expand business-to-business engagement."
  },
