    "md5": "262d424e9b9c1e3ea1d7da2e7cc2af72",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1787,
    "chunk_text": "An Israel that is left free to do what it wants will be a permanent threat to every country in the Middle East. It is to defend themselves from a rogue State, that Saudi Arabia, Turkiye and Pakistan have forged the Mecca alliance.\n\nIt is significant that the US has not objected to the Mecca Pact. It would want its defence responsibilities in West Asia off its shoulders. Israel, as expected, feels threatened by the pact. It has said that the pact will push normalisation with Saudi Arabia further out of reach. And Israel has always considered Turkiye a threat to it on par with Iran.\n\nIsrael is expected to respond along two parallel axes-strengthen its existing Mediterranean alliance with Greece and Cyprus, and form a new counter pact with the United Arab Emirates (UAE) and India. Israel already has a strong defence relationship with India.\n\nAn Israel that is left free to do what it wants will be a permanent threat to every country in the Middle East\n\nMs Oshrit Birvadker, a senior research fellow at the Jerusalem Institute for Strategy and Security (JISS) writes in www.israelhayom.com to say that the Mecca Pact is a \u2018Muslim NATO\u2019. It marks a strategic turning point in the Middle East and South Asia, bringing together the custodian of Islam\u2019s holiest sites (Saudi Arabia), a nuclear power (Pakistan) and a NATO member (T\u00fcrkiye). This combination is fit enough to accelerate the regional and global arms race.\n\nThe development poses significant challenges for Israel, pushes the prospect of normalisation with Saudi Arabia further out of reach and cuts short the vision of a \u201cnew Middle East\u201d Envisaged by the Abraham Accords. Israel\u2019s appropriate response should be to immediately tighten coordination with the United Arab Emirates and India, Birvadker says."
