    "md5": "5a8be6a649e16d75f6fb6dd37c372476",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1904,
    "chunk_text": "NCE to lead exporters\u2019 delegation to India to unlock new market opportunities\n\nSri Lankan exporters invited to join business delegation to New Delhi and Mumbai from September 24 to October 01, 2026\n\nThe National Chamber of Exporters of Sri Lanka (NCE) is inviting the exporters, manufacturers, aspiring exporters and other businesses interested in expanding into the Indian market to join an overseas exporters\u2019 delegation to New Delhi and Mumbai, from September 24 to October 01, 2026.\n\nIndia is one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most important trading partners and presents significant opportunities for expanding Sri Lankan exports. In 2025, Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to India increased by 17.2 percent to approximately US $ 1.04 billion, compared with US $ 881.6 million in 2024. The positive momentum has continued in 2026, with the exports to India increasing by 36.16 percent to US $ 688.47 million during the first six months of the year.\n\nWith a population exceeding 1.4 billion and a rapidly expanding consumer and business economy, India offers considerable opportunities for Sri Lankan companies across multiple sectors. These include tea, rubber and rubber-based products, coconut products, spices, apparel and textiles, food and beverages, gems and jewellery, electrical and electronic products, ICT and BPM services, logistics, manufacturing and other value-added products and services.\n\nThere are also opportunities beyond traditional exports, including joint ventures, investment, contract manufacturing, distribution partnerships, technology collaboration and integration into Indian and regional supply chains.\n\nThe Sri Lankan exporters have the advantage of the India Sri Lanka Free Trade Agreement (ISFTA), which has provided preferential market access since 2000. In 2025, approximately US $ 634 million or 61.3 percent of Sri Lanka\u2019s exports to India, were exported under the ISFTA framework."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
