    "description": "Inflation rises for fourth straight month to 7.2% in July",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Inflation-rises-for-fourth-straight-month-to-7-2-in-July/215-348650",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787382137.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-22-dailymirrorlk-22b6bfd9-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "499e4ee5e1ace05aa28b751a048ac6c9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1792,
    "chunk_text": "Inflation rises for fourth straight month to 7.2% in July\n\nNational Consumer Price Index rose 0.5% MoM to 223.4 in July, significantly slower than 1.6% monthly increase recorded in June\n\nComposition of inflation showed that pressure on household budgets remained concentrated outside food\n\nNon-food inflation stood at 9.2% year-on-year while food inflation accelerated sharply to 4.9%, from 3.3%\n\nThe nationwide inflation accelerated to 7.2 percent in July, from 6.5 percent in June, as the higher non-food costs continued to account for the bulk of price pressures, the latest data from the Census and Statistics Department showed.\n\nThe National Consumer Price Index (NCPI) rose 0.5 percent month-on-month (MoM) to 223.4 in July, significantly slower than the 1.6 percent monthly increase recorded in June. The combination points to a continued acceleration in annual inflation even as fresh price pressures moderated during the month.\n\nThe composition of inflation showed that the pressure on the household budgets remained concentrated outside food. Non-food inflation stood at 9.2 percent year-on-year in July, marginally easing from 9.3 percent in June, while food inflation accelerated sharply to 4.9 percent, from 3.3 percent.\n\nThe non-food items contributed 5.04 percentage points to the 7.2 percent headline inflation rate, more than double the 2.21 percentage-point contribution from food, according to the Census and Statistics Department.\n\nTransport was the largest source of annual non-food inflation, contributing 2.23 percentage points, followed by housing, water, electricity, gas and other fuels at 1.21 percentage points. Restaurants and hotels contributed 0.50 percentage points, education 0.35 percentage points and miscellaneous goods and services 0.26 percentage points."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-08-22-dailymirrorlk-22b6bfd9",
    "num": "dailymirrorlk-22b6bfd9",
    "date_str": "2026-08-22",
    "description": "Inflation rises for fourth straight month to 7.2% in July",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business/Inflation-rises-for-fourth-straight-month-to-7-2-in-July/215-348650",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787382137.0,
