    "md5": "5ee3cddd20fcf3730a2f68016618dc4c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1782,
    "chunk_text": "Paredes receives 10-game suspension, three Argentina players punished by FIFA following World Cup final fallout\n\nAUG.22 - Argentina\u2019s Leandro Paredes has been handed a ten\u2011match suspension by FIFA for his role in a post\u2011match brawl following the 2026 World Cup final defeat to Spain in New Jersey.\n\nArgentina midfielder Leandro Paredes was slapped with a ten-match suspension for his involvement in a brawl after his side lost to Spain in the 2026 World Cup final in New Jersey, as FIFA announced on Friday.\n\nThe global football federation also sanctioned defender Nahuel Molina with a seven\u2011match ban, while Thiago Almada received a one\u2011game suspension.\n\nParedes was sanctioned for his involvement in a post-match brawl when he shoved Gavi to the ground and grabbed Eric Garcia by the throat as the Spanish players came onto the pitch to celebrate.\n\nFIFA imposed brutal sanctions on the Argentine players, with Paredes facing three assault counts and Molina facing two. Almada and Gavi also faced a count each for unsportsmanlike behaviour, while Argentina assistant coach Roberto Ayala faced an assault count.\n\nThe global football body also imposed heavy fines, with Paredes and Molina being fined USD 90,000 each while Almada and coach Ayala were slapped with a USD 30,000 fine.\n\nParedes\u2019 suspension effectively amounts to a year\u2011long expulsion from the Argentina squad, as FIFA\u2019s calendar through June 2027 features ten fixtures. All of them are international friendlies, with no competitive matches scheduled.\n\nThe punishment for Paredes is among the most severe ones in World Cup history.\n\nApart from the Argentina players, Gavi was also handed a one-game suspension. He will miss out on Spain's Nations League clash against England on September 26 at Wembley."
