    "chunk_size_bytes": 1591,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lankan Podcasters convene for landmark media landscape forum in Colombo\n\nColombo, August 22 (Daily Mirror) - The Podcasters\u2019 Association of Sri Lanka recently hosted a high-level discussion titled \"Exploring the New Media Landscape\" at the Granbell Hotel in Colombo. Bringing together over 100 digital content creators, media professionals, and industry stakeholders, the event focused on the central theme of navigating structural challenges, identifying new opportunities, and fostering sustainable growth for the nation's creator economy.\n\nDelivering the keynote address, Deputy Minister of Mass Media Dr. Kaushalya Ariyarathne emphasized the government's strong commitment to supporting the evolving digital media space. She highlighted the vital role that independent content creators play in modern information dissemination, reaffirming the state's dedication to creating a responsible, thriving ecosystem for digital platforms and communicators.\n\nAssociation President and Attorney-at-Law Namini Panditha underscored podcasting's power in driving civic engagement and promoting transparency across politics, economics, and governance. She noted that digital and traditional media complement one another rather than compete, urging both sectors to collaborate closely, set high industry benchmarks, and tap into economic opportunities. Additionally, founding member Bruno Diwakara reflected on the rapid journey of local digital content creation, emphasizing the importance of a unified association to elevate professional standards and ensure long-term industry sustainability."
