    "md5": "b21245be03409636a430988a816c2f57",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1985,
    "chunk_text": "Govt committed to equal rights and opportunities for all: PM\n\nColombo, August 22 (Daily Mirror) - Ensuring equal rights and equal opportunities for all citizens, without leaving anyone behind, is a fundamental policy of the Government, Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuriya said.\n\nThe Prime Minister made these remarks today (22) while attending the \u201cSarasavi Diriya Abhiman\u201d ceremony organised by the President\u2019s Fund at the Jaffna District Secretariat Auditorium to recognise university students with disabilities.\n\nAt the event, 75 university students with disabilities from the Northern Province were presented with certificates of appreciation and a cash award of Rs. 100,000 each.\n\nAddressing the gathering, Prime Minister Amarasuriya said the programme was being implemented to recognise students with disabilities pursuing university education across the country and to encourage many more young people to overcome challenges and pursue their educational aspirations.\n\nShe said the Northern and Eastern provinces have a significant number of persons with disabilities, including those affected by the country\u2019s past conflict.\n\n\u201cWe are working to build a society where everyone has equal opportunities and where no one is left behind. Bringing the President\u2019s Fund closer to the people is an important part of that effort,\u201d she said.\n\nThe Prime Minister acknowledged that the journey of students with disabilities towards higher education was often more challenging, as they had to overcome physical barriers as well as social and attitudinal barriers.\n\nShe commended the students for their determination and said their achievements demonstrated the strength and resilience needed to overcome challenges.\n\n\u201cThe fact that you are standing here today as university students is a testament to your determination and strength.\n\nYour journey is an example to the younger generation, particularly those who become discouraged when faced with difficulties,\u201d she said."
  },
