    "chunk_text": "8-year-old girl dies in Walpola accident\n\nColombo, Aug. 23 (Daily Mirror) - An 8-year-old girl has died following a tragic multi-vehicle accident near the Walpola railway crossing on the Ragama\u2013Kandana road on Saturday (August 22).\n\nAccording to the police, the accident occurred when a garbage transport lorry travelling from the direction of Walpola Temple toward Walpola Railway Station reportedly lost control while the railway crossing gates were closed.\n\nThe lorry subsequently crashed into two parked cars and another lorry near the railway crossing.\n\nAt the time of the incident, a mother and her two children \u2014 a son and an 8-year-old daughter \u2014 were walking along the roadside. All three were injured in the collision and were rushed to Ragama Teaching Hospital for treatment.\n\nHowever, the young girl succumbed to her injuries while undergoing treatment at the hospital.\n\nFollowing the accident, the driver of one of the lorries involved was taken into police custody. The driver of the garbage transport lorry was also admitted to Ragama Hospital after reportedly suffering a sudden illness.\n\nPolice in Ragama are continuing investigations into the circumstances surrounding the accident."
