    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1787506157.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-08-23-dailymirrorlk-1cc3bb6c-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "c311b894ba00100e568a122563aae4cf",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1724,
    "chunk_text": "ComBank named SL\u2019s Strongest Banking Brand by Brand Finance AAA rating\n\nSanath Manatunge, Managing Director/CEO of Commercial Bank receives the Strongest Banking Brand plaque from Anuk Wijeyeratne, Managing Director of Brand Finance Lanka\n\nReflecting its unwavering stability and the enduring trust of customers, Commercial Bank of Ceylon has once again reaffirmed its leadership as Sri Lanka\u2019s Strongest Banking Brand in Brand Finance\u2019s newest \u2018100 Most Valuable Brands 2026\u2019 report.\n\nAccording to the latest rankings published by the world\u2019s leading brand valuation consultancy, Commercial Bankhas also been ranked the 2nd Most Valuable Brand in the country overall, withits brand value computed at Rs. 54.9 billion, representing a significant increase of 17.8 percent over last year\u2019s valuation of Rs. 46.6 billion.\n\nIn terms of brand strength, the Bank has achieved a Brand Strength Index (BSI) score of 87 out of 100 and has once again been awarded the prestigious AAA rating by Brand Finance. The Bank\u2019s positions in both brand value and brand strength rankings remain unchanged from the previous year, underscoring the consistency and resilience of its brand performance.\n\nCommenting on the Bank\u2019s performance in the 2026 rankings, Sanath Manatunge, Managing Director/CEO of Commercial Bank said, \u201cReaffirming our position as the No. 1 bank brand in brand strength with a prestigious AAA rating, alongsidea substantial increase in brand value is a clear reflection of the strength, stability and trust that define Commercial Bank. These rankings reaffirm the enduring confidence placed in the Bank by our stakeholders and highlight the effectiveness of our long-term approach to brand building.\u201d"
  },
