    "chunk_text": "Changes in the surrounding area are also visible through land values and patterns of development. The study identifies a real increase of more than 830 percent in land values since NSBM\u2019s establishment, while satellite-derived nighttime light data shows a substantial increase in light intensity around the campus between 2013 and 2026.\n\nTogether with the business survey findings, these indicators highlight the broader transformation of Homagama, Pitipana into an emerging education and services hub.\n\nNSBM\u2019s sustainability and social impact also extend beyond the boundaries of the campus. Between 2021 and 2026, the university has undertaken approximately 233 CSR initiatives, covering environmental conservation, education, community infrastructure and social development. These initiatives have included biodiversity conservation, tree planting, beach clean-ups, recycling initiatives, school gardens, sanitation improvements and educational support.\n\nTaken together, the findings of the study done by Deloitte demonstrate that the value created by a university cannot be measured solely by the number of students it educates or the degrees it awards.\n\nNSBM\u2019s impact is created through several interconnected channels: developing skilled graduates, creating and supporting employment, stimulating local businesses, retaining foreign exchange, encouraging entrepreneurship, supporting investment and contributing to environmental and community development.\n\nAs NSBM enters its next phase of development, this contribution has the potential to deepen further. The university\u2019s ongoing expansion includes new academic infrastructure and the proposed NSBM Medical Research and Teaching Hospital, which is expected to broaden the institution\u2019s contribution into healthcare education, clinical training, research and related economic activity."
