    "language": "en",
    "md5": "73eaeb6ec207c07d401ca27757ae9872",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1921,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank sustains strong growth momentum with Rs. 32.6bn record pre-tax profit in 1H 2026\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank continued its growth during the six months ended June 30, 2026, delivering profitability supported by core banking performance, improved margins, and disciplined financial management.\n\nThe bank recorded a standalone Profit Before Tax (PBT) of Rs. 32.6 billion for the period, alongside a record Profit After Tax of Rs 20.5 billion.\n\nTotal operating income increased by 17.7 percent to Rs 95.2 billion, compared to Rs 80.9 billion in the same period last year, while net interest income grew by 18.9 percent to Rs 82.4 billion from Rs 69.3 billion. The Net Interest Margin (NIM) increased to 4.4 percent from 4.1 percent. Total assets stabilized at Rs 3.8 trillion, and gross loans and advances surpassed the Rs 2.0 trillion milestone for the first time, reaching Rs 2.1 trillion.\n\nThe Total Capital Adequacy Ratio improved to 18.2 percent by June 30, 2026, compared to 17.9% at the end of the first quarter and 16.5 percent at the end of 2025. The Tier I Capital Adequacy Ratio stood at 12.7 percent. Liquidity remained stable, with the All Currency Liquidity Coverage Ratio at 212.3 percent and the Rupee Liquidity Coverage Ratio at 255.9 percent.\n\nAt the Group level, Profit Before Tax was Rs 37.4 billion, representing a 20.6 percent growth compared to Rs 31.0 billion in the previous year. Group total assets stabilised at Rs 4.1 trillion, while gross loans and advances increased to Rs 2.4 trillion. Group net interest income grew by 22.9 percent to Rs. 97.0 billion from Rs 79.0 billion, and Group Net Interest Margin improved to 4.8 percent from 4.4 percent.\n\nChairman Narada Fernando stated, \u201cPeople\u2019s Bank has continued to demonstrate strength, resilience and financial stability despite a complex global environment shaped by geopolitical developments and persistent economic uncertainties.\u201d"
  },
