    "chunk_size_bytes": 1762,
    "chunk_text": "Vogue Jewellers ropes in Kumar Sangakkara to drive global expansion\n\nVogue Jewellers Managing Director Anura Hemachandra presenting Kumar Sangakkara with a specially crafted golden cricket bat\n\nVogue Jewellers, one of Sri Lanka\u2019s premier jewellery houses, has formally signed former national captain Kumar Sangakkara as its brand ambassador, entering a strategic partnership aimed at strengthening its international footprint and reinforcing brand equity across key global markets.\n\nThe partnership marks a pivotal milestone for the six-decade-old brand as it accelerates its overseas footprint, exactly one year after establishing its first overseas showroom at Westfield Fountain Gate in Melbourne, Australia, in August 2025.\n\nThe collaboration brings together two globally recognised Sri Lankan names underpinned by an uncompromising pursuit of excellence, integrity, and long-term value creation.\n\nSpeaking at the official signing ceremony held in Colombo last week, Vogue Jewellers Managing Director Anura Hemachandra described the alliance as a natural alignment of principles that have stood the test of time. He noted that the company had long envisioned bringing Sangakkara on board, tracing their connection back nearly two decades to an exhibition in 2008 where Sangakkara first commended the brand\u2019s dedication to craftsmanship and consumer education.\n\n\u201cThis is much more than an association between a brand and an ambassador. Kumar and Vogue represent two distinctly Sri Lankan journeys that have earned recognition beyond our shores.\n\nWhat connects those journeys is a relentless pursuit of excellence, a respect for one\u2019s craft and, above all, the understanding that a reputation of lasting value is built over time,\u201d Hemachandra stated."
  },
