    "chunk_text": "What connects those journeys is a relentless pursuit of excellence, a respect for one\u2019s craft and, above all, the understanding that a reputation of lasting value is built over time,\u201d Hemachandra stated.\n\n\u201cWhen I joined this business six years ago officially, one of the things my father told me was to take this legacy overseas. We opened up a showroom in Melbourne, and we intend to do what this gentleman did on cricket. We want to be the first and the pioneer in the jewellery industry to take this country and compete with foreign brands,\u201d Anuradha Hemachandra said.\n\nHowever, he remained tight-lipped regarding specific target markets to protect the company\u2019s strategic advantage.\n\n\u201cWith regards to the expansion, we do have a few countries in mind, but obviously, I can\u2019t reveal what those countries are because of the competitive edge,\u201d he explained, adding that there are no immediate plans for further local investments.\n\nAddressing the macro-operating environment, he noted that while fluctuating international gold prices remain dictated by external factors like Middle Eastern conflicts and US dollar movements, jewellery continues to serve as an enduring store of wealth and an effective hedge against inflation. He emphasised that unwavering adherence to purity standards and consumer trust remain strictly non-negotiable pillars of Vogue\u2019s business model.\n\nKumar Sangakkara, whose associations have remained highly selective throughout his career, noted that the foundation of any lasting partnership must be rooted in shared values and emotional resonance rather than transactional endorsements.\n\n\u201cOver time I matured a lot in that sense and understood that longer-lasting partnerships based on trust and shared values are much more important than anything else,\u201d Sangakkara said. \u201cIt\u2019s a brand I respect, built on incredible trust from the people, and they create beautiful things that last a lifetime.\u201d"
