    "chunk_text": "Long afterwards, Buddhist monks led by the late Kosgoda Dhammawansa appealed to Jayewardene to restore Bandaranaike\u2019s civic rights. He recalled his son\u2019s detention during the 1971 insurgency. Asked whether his actions were revenge, he did not answer. Yet the strategy was larger than personal retaliation: it was aimed at preventing a powerful rival from returning to the political battlefield.\n\n\u201cUnjust, unfair, and revengeful\u201d actions can ultimately boomerang on those who wield power. The old warning remains relevant: when the One Great Scorer writes against your name, he records not whether you won or lost, but how you played the game."
