    "chunk_id": "2026-08-24-dailyftlk-b3679c68-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "978d1e69ab4772be556feeb6b05a6832",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1852,
    "chunk_text": "PAQS 2026: Connecting  Sri Lanka\u2019s quantity surveying profession  to the region\n\nAs Sri Lanka prepares to host the PAQS Congress 2026 this week, the country\u2019s Quantity Surveying profession is presented with an opportunity to engage more closely with its regional counterparts, share knowledge and demonstrate the strength of its professional community. The Daily FT spoke to the Institute of Quantity Surveyors of Sri Lanka (IQSSL) Immediate Past President Indunil Seneviratne and PAQS Past President, Emeritus Professor Chitra Weddikkara on the significance of PAQS, the global mobility of Sri Lankan Quantity Surveyors, the role of technology and the profession\u2019s contribution to the wider economy\n\nQ: For those outside the profession, what is PAQS and why does it matter?\n\nSeneviratne: The Pacific Association of Quantity Surveyors is a regional body representing Quantity Surveyors in the Asia-Pacific region, with Sri Lanka represented by the IQSSL. PAQS provides a platform for regulating education, research and the sharing of research outcomes among member countries. It also accredits undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in areas such as cost management and Quantity Surveying. This recognition provides global mobility for graduates, allowing a person qualifying in Sri Lanka to pursue opportunities in countries such as Australia, New Zealand, Japan and Hong Kong.\n\nProf. Weddikkara: I would describe PAQS as a bridge that connects Quantity Surveying professionals across different countries. The building sector is becoming increasingly multinational, with projects, consultants, contractors, investors and technologies crossing national borders. PAQS gives professional institutions an opportunity to connect, share knowledge and experiences, learn from one another and collectively strengthen the profession across the region."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
