    "chunk_size_bytes": 1812,
    "chunk_text": "Govt. launches data platforms for fisheries, plantation sectors via IDAT Program\n\nThe Government has advanced a key national digital transformation priority through the launch and handover of Decision Support Systems for the fisheries and plantation sectors under the Inclusive Digital Agriculture Transformation Program, known as IDAT. The Government-led initiative is designed to strengthen how public institutions collect, integrate and use data to guide policy, planning, resource allocation and service delivery.\n\nThe Fisheries Sector Decision Support System brings together data from six Government institutions: the National Aquaculture Development Authority, Ceylon Fisheries Harbours Corporation, Ceylon Fisheries Corporation, Cey-Nor Foundation, North Sea Ltd. and the Central Fish Market (Colombo).\n\nThe platform provides integrated datasets, dashboards, visual analytics, reports, monitoring tools and alerts to support decisions relating to fisheries production, aquaculture, market intelligence, operational performance, sustainability and resource management. Its development included institutional consultations, system design, analytical development, validation, capacity building, user acceptance testing and production-readiness activities.\n\n\u201cThe Fisheries DSS represents an important step in modernising sector governance through reliable data and evidence-based decision-making. By bringing institutional data together, the platform strengthens planning, monitoring, forecasting and resource management across the fisheries sector. This initiative will strengthen institutional efficiency, transparency and responsiveness while supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda,\u201d said Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources Ministry Secretary Dr. B.K. Kolita Kamal Jinadasa."
  },
