    "chunk_size_bytes": 1600,
    "chunk_text": "\u201cThe Fisheries DSS represents an important step in modernising sector governance through reliable data and evidence-based decision-making. By bringing institutional data together, the platform strengthens planning, monitoring, forecasting and resource management across the fisheries sector. This initiative will strengthen institutional efficiency, transparency and responsiveness while supporting Sri Lanka\u2019s broader digital transformation agenda,\u201d said Fisheries, Aquatic and Ocean Resources Ministry Secretary Dr. B.K. Kolita Kamal Jinadasa.\n\n\u201cThe Plantation DSS marks an important step in strengthening evidence-based governance, enabling institutions to make better-informed decisions through integrated data and analytics. The platform will strengthen institutional coordination, operational efficiency and long-term planning across Sri Lanka\u2019s plantation sector. This initiative demonstrates how collaboration and digital public infrastructure can support a more competitive, resilient and sustainable plantation economy,\u201d said Plantation and Community Infrastructure Ministry Secretary Gunadasa Samarasinghe.\n\nThrough a single Government-owned platform, decision-makers can monitor the performance of tea, rubber, coconut and cashew, assess district-level trends, review exports, track investments and subsidy programs, understand climate and weather-related impacts and identify areas requiring timely intervention. The platform is intended to help Government institutions better target programs and investments while monitoring progress against national development priorities."
  },
