    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "79740f0cd6a3cca6847415bde2e4e2d2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1677,
    "chunk_text": "President orders faster rollout of Rs.102 b provincial Ditwah projects\n\nPresident Anura Kumara Dissanayake has instructed officials to accelerate projects being implemented by Provincial Councils using Rs. 102 billion allocated from the Government\u2019s Rs. 500 billion provision for the Ditwah disaster situation.\n\nThe directive was issued during a meeting at the Presidential Secretariat on Friday to review the progress of development projects being implemented by Provincial Councils under 2026 Budget allocations and preparations for the 2027 Budget, the President\u2019s Media Division (PMD) said.\n\nAccording to the PMD, 30,923 development projects are currently being implemented at provincial level, covering sectors including education, health, agriculture, livestock and irrigation. The meeting reviewed their progress and implementation issues.\n\nPresident Dissanayake called for the Central Government and Provincial Councils to implement projects within a unified policy framework while adhering to their respective responsibilities. He also called for improved sharing of data and coordination across State institutions to prevent project duplication and expenditure on unnecessary projects.\n\nThe President also instructed officials to ensure that projects financed through foreign loans and assistance are completed on schedule and deliver their intended benefits.\n\nWith preparations for the 2027 Budget underway, President Dissanayake stressed the need to maintain financial discipline and operate within prescribed expenditure limits. He instructed officials to complete planning for all projects by November so that implementation could begin on schedule next year."
  },
