    "chunk_size_bytes": 1796,
    "chunk_text": "What\u2019s in the Imran Khan letter? Sunil Gavaskar, Arjuna and others make three key requests\n\nTIMES OF INDIA - Former captains Sunil Gavaskar, Kapil Dev, Arjuna Ranatunga and Nasser Hussain are among 21 former international cricket captains who have written to Pakistan Prime Minister Shehbaz Sharif, asking for proper medical treatment and welfare of jailed former Pakistan Prime Minister and World Cup-winning captain Imran Khan.\n\nThe letter was initiated by former Australia captain Greg Chappell. It is the second appeal by former international captains seeking humane treatment and medical care for the 73-year-old Khan.\n\nThe captains said they were \"not seek to adjudicate Pakistan\u2019s domestic legal processes but believed that ensuring a court-ordered medical process was completed was a basic matter of decency\".\n\nThe former captains made three specific requests to the Pakistan government:\n\nThey asked that the medical board ordered by Pakistan's Supreme Court, including Imran Khan's personal doctors, be allowed to complete a full and independent assessment of his health, especially the reported loss of vision in his right eye.\n\nThe captains urged the government to honour the Supreme Court's order allowing Khan's family to meet him every week without interruption or administrative delays.\n\nThey requested that any medical treatment recommended after the assessment be provided without delay.\n\nKhan has been in jail since 2023. Late last year, he and his wife were sentenced to 17 years in prison on corruption charges, which they both deny.\n\nOn Friday, Khan was taken back to jail just hours after being moved to Islamabad's private Shifa International Hospital for medical checks ordered by the Supreme Court. His lawyers had approached the court over concerns about his health."
