    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "Lankan drug lord questioned by FBI over Iran links before deportation\n\nColombo, Aug. 24 (Daily Mirror) - While Sri Lankan authorities continue to investigate notorious drug trafficker Shiran Basik\u2019s alleged drug empire, illicit assets and international links, the Daily Mirror learns that Basik was also questioned in Dubai by FBI agents over possible connections to Iran before he was eventually handed over to Sri Lankan authorities.\n\nBasik, who was arrested by Dubai Police on May 26, 2026, reportedly came under the attention of US authorities after photographs and videos of Iranian drones and missiles were allegedly found on his mobile phone. Given his alleged links to international drug trafficking networks and the potential security implications, US agencies questioned him to determine whether he had any political or security-related connections to Iran.\n\nHowever, the inquiries were subsequently dropped after US authorities reportedly determined that Basik\u2019s connections to Iran were linked to drug trafficking networks rather than political or security activities.\n\nAs a result, the US agencies did not pursue further action against him, paving the way for his eventual deportation to Sri Lanka.\n\nDubai authorities later deported Basik to Sri Lanka on August 14 under heavy security. Later the Central Crimes Investigation Bureau (CCIB) has obtained a 90-day detention order to further interrogate Basik.\n\nSri Lankan authorities are now investigating his alleged drug trafficking operations, financial networks and assets believed to have been acquired through illicit activities. The investigations are being conducted with the involvement of the Central Bank of Sri Lanka, with authorities examining his bank accounts and other financial transactions.\n\nDuring questioning, Basik reportedly provided information about additional properties allegedly linked to him. Police said he disclosed that he owns two houses and two mobile phone shops in Boralesgamuwa."
