    "chunk_text": "The audit further found that fuel consumption for the three official vehicles assigned to the Deputy Speaker exceeded the applicable limits by 6,980 litres in 2023. In 2024, two official vehicles exceeded the prescribed limits by a further 1,515 litres.\n\nThe audit also examined the vehicle use and fuel consumption of the Secretary-General of Parliament. It found that two official vehicles had been used simultaneously by the Secretary-General during 2022 and 2023, with vehicle logbooks confirming that both were in operation during overlapping periods.\n\nThe Secretary-General was also not subject to a specific fuel limit. The audit found that 15,063 litres of fuel, valued at approximately Rs. 6.07 million, had been used between 2022 and 2024.\n\nThis amounted to an annual average of around 5,031 litres, which the audit noted was approximately 2,300 litres more per year than the fuel allocation provided to a Ministry Secretary, who falls within the highest fuel-entitlement category in the public service."
