    "md5": "f222452ae032f7b84757b95ac8ccf8c4",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 977,
    "chunk_text": "Eric Meyer arrives to take up U.S. Ambassador post\n\nColombo, Aug. 24 (Daily Mirror) - U.S. Ambassador-designate to Sri Lanka Eric Meyer arrived in Colombo to assume his duties as the 29th United States Ambassador to Sri Lanka.\n\nMeyer said he was honoured to represent the United States in Sri Lanka and looked forward to further strengthening ties between the two countries.\n\n\u201cIt is an honor to represent the United States in Sri Lanka. I look forward to building on the strong foundation between our two democracies to advance a U.S.-Sri Lanka partnership that creates new opportunities for American businesses, furthers our shared security interests, and delivers greater prosperity for both Americans and Sri Lankans,\u201d he said.\n\nBefore his appointment to Sri Lanka, Meyer served as Charg\u00e9 d\u2019Affaires, a.i. at the U.S. Mission to Norway.\n\nHe previously served as Senior Bureau Official for the Bureau of South and Central Asian Affairs at the U.S. Department of State."
