    "chunk_size_bytes": 1972,
    "chunk_text": "Another dimension that cannot be ignored is the growing culture among some young officials of seeking instant wealth and overnight success at any cost. When legitimate achievement is replaced by the pursuit of quick money, fraud, bribery, money laundering and financial manipulation can become dangerously normalized. Sri Lanka must confront this mindset by strengthening financial ethics, accountability and awareness\u2014because a society that glorifies unexplained wealth risks creating a generation that values money over integrity.\n\nThis confidence is fragile. A banking system perceived as vulnerable to insider collusion, fraudulent documentation and large-scale capital flight risks damaging not only individual banks but also Sri Lanka\u2019s reputation as an international financial and investment destination.\n\nThe country therefore needs more than prosecutions. It needs a fundamental strengthening of financial governance.\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s banks are custodians of the country\u2019s financial security not gateways for capital flight. Customers who deliberately manipulate the system must face the full force of the law. Bank employees who knowingly facilitate such transactions must be held individually accountable. Institutions that fail to maintain effective controls must face meaningful regulatory consequences.\n\nThe billions allegedly taken out of the country must not disappear into the international financial system.\n\nPresent investigation has exposed a dangerous vulnerability. The country\u2019s response will determine whether this episode becomes another chapter in Sri Lanka\u2019s history of financial scandals or the moment when the nation finally draws a line under weak controls, institutional complacency and impunity.\n\nThe question is no longer simply whether money was illegally taken out of Sri Lanka.\n\nThe question is whether Sri Lanka is prepared to protect every dollar that remains\u2014and restore the confidence that its banking system must command."
